o shape your own go-to-market with local partners and AI-assisted research.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The impact you will have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Open new private sector accounts across CEE and Central Asia. Working with internal and external stakeholders to build effective networks to deliver commercial execution of TRM’s services to leading private sector organisations across the region.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Win a mixture of high velocity and larger more strategic engagements, by turning AML and fraud pain points into a clear business case, with AI-drafted account plans and proposals that you sharpen with your own market judgment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and define the model to build a 3x qualified pipeline each quarter through targeted campaigns, using AI-assisted segmentation and local-language messaging, and measure what converts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Decide how TRM enters each market, choosing between direct selling, resellers, and regional partners, and back each choice with AI-assisted analysis of account data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grow strategic existing customers engagements through renewals, upsells, and new use cases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring customer and regulatory insight back to Product and Marketing so the next release matches how banks in your region actually work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years selling SaaS or data products into banks, payment firms, crypto or fintechs in CEE or Central Asia, or 4+ years with deep AML and financial crime expertise, plus experience using AI tools to research and prioritize accounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A record of closing a mixture of quick deal cycle and strategic longer term, higher value engagements and meeting quota, with AI-supported forecasting and pipeline reviews.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of regional AML and sanctions frameworks and how compliance, risk, and procurement teams buy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on use of AI for prospecting, account planning, and call preparation, with clear examples of time or revenue gained.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building pipeline in a new territory, forming human lead networks and AI-assisted tools to test and measure what works.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Credible, clear communication with senior compliance and risk executives, in person and virtually, including AI-assisted preparation for each meeting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English; Russian or a CEE relevant language is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Based in Poland and willingness to travel regularly across the region.</strong></em></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Team:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">TRM’s EMEA Sales team gives each Account Director full ownership of a territory and the room to choose how to win it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The team collaborates closely and supports one another through shared pipeline insight, deal reviews, and open sharing of what works.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The work is hard in a useful way: regulated buyers, several countries, long procurement cycles, and a product category that is still new to many banks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work with RevOps, Marketing, Legal, Product, and Solutions Architecture, who move quickly to back your deals.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learn about TRM Speed in this position:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Within your first 30 days, you rank every target bank and fintech in your territory and start outreach to the top tier, so pipeline grows before onboarding ends.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">When a compliance leader asks for a demo late on a Friday, you and TRM’s Solutions team deliver it that day, turning a warm inquiry into a scheduled evaluation by Monday.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Within 90 days, you build qualified pipeline worth at least 3x your quota, backed by an account plan for every Tier 1 target.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Operating Rhythms:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Distributed, not distant: the team works across UK and CET time zones, with flexibility for Central Asia hours and occasional US calls on complex deals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Slack is the center of day-to-day communication. @mention colleagues for timely responses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Weekly 1:1 with your manager, a weekly team call, a weekly pipeline call, a weekly forecast call, and regular pod calls.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company-wide all-hands and founder Q&amp;A sessions keep everyone connected to the mission.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Required online and collaboration hours:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Schedule: Core hours overlapping CET, with flexibility for Central Asia hours and occasional US calls. </p></li></ul><h2><strong>Application Instructions</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re interested in joining TRM, we encourage you to apply directly. Every application is reviewed by our Talent team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Before applying, review the job description carefully and highlight the experience and impact that best demonstrate the required qualifications. Please also provide thoughtful and accurate answers to the application questions, as these will be used to evaluate your skills and qualifications for the role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you send your resume directly to someone at TRM, we can’t guarantee it will reach the appropriate hiring team. Applying directly is the best way to ensure your application will be considered.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Interviewing with TRM</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our process is designed to understand how you think, solve problems, and deliver impact, while allowing you to evaluate TRM. Most interview processes include a case study, an AI skills assessment, and a Leadership Principles interview.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Recruiter Intro:</strong> Qualifications, motivations, and alignment with the role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hiring Manager:</strong> Deep dive into your relevant experience, skills, and impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First Round:</strong> 1–2 interviews focused on the skills most critical to the role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final Round: </strong>Hands-on case study. This is usually a panel-style session where we go deeper into your craft, problem-solving, and alignment with TRM.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>References:</strong> Former colleagues who can provide insight into your work and impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Offer:</strong> Congrats! Your recruiter will present the offer and compensation details.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Welcome to TRM:</strong> We're excited to build a safer world with you!</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your recruiter will share your specific interview plan and preparation guidance along the way.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>AI Fluency at TRM</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI fluency is a baseline expectation at TRM.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe AI meaningfully changes how top performers operate. We expect every team member to use AI to accelerate and reimagine their craft, not just automate surface tasks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At TRM, AI fluency means you are among the top 10 percent of operators in your function in how you apply AI to:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accelerate repeatable workflows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Structure and solve problems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve output quality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Increase speed and leverage</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be evaluated on applied AI fluency during the interview process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Life at TRM</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are building a safer world. That promise shows up in how we work every day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">TRM moves FAST. We are a high-velocity, high-ownership team that expects clarity, follow-through, and impact. People who thrive here are energized by hard problems, experimentation, and continuous feedback. If something takes months elsewhere, it will ship here in days.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work sits at the intersection of AI, national security, and fighting crime. The problems are complex, the stakes are real, and the environment evolves quickly. The pace and intensity of the work reflect the importance of the mission. As a result, the way we operate requires a high level of ownership, adaptability, collaboration, and creative problem-solving.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At TRM, you should expect:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Priorities and targets to change quickly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operating with a high degree of ambiguity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A high level of personal ownership and accountability</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Close collaboration across teams and functions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Frequent, high-touch communication</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Creative problem-solving and out-of-the-box thinking</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A pace that rewards urgency, adaptability, and outcomes</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">This environment is energizing for people who enjoy building, solving hard problems, and making progress in situations that are not always fully defined. It also requires thriving in ambiguity, adjusting course as new information emerges, and maintaining focus and positivity in a fast-moving and intense environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We also recognize that this style of operating is not for everyone. If you are primarily optimizing for predictability or a consistently balanced workload, we encourage you to use the interview process to pressure-test whether this environment is truly the right fit. We want teammates who thrive here, not just survive here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you are excited by meaningful problems, motivated by ambitious goals, and energized by working alongside mission-driven colleagues, there is a good chance you will find TRM to be an exceptional place to grow and contribute. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Leadership Principles</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We hire and grow against three leadership principles. They’re the standards for how we operate, treat each other, and make decisions.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Impact-Oriented Trailblazer: We put customers first and move with speed, focus, and adaptability. We treat every plan like an experiment – test, ship, measure, and iterate quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Master Craftsperson: We care deeply about our craft. We balance speed with high standards, own outcomes end‑to‑end, and invest in getting better everyday.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Inspiring Colleague: We add clarity and energy, not noise. We bring humility, candor, and a one‑team mindset — giving and receiving feedback to make the team stronger.</p></li></ul><h3></h3><h2><strong>Join our Mission</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At TRM, we care deeply about our craft. We are looking for individuals who want their work to matter, who experiment with speed and rigor, and who take pride in building a safer world for billions of people. If you’re excited by TRM’s mission but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply — we hire for slope, judgment, and the will to learn fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">TRM is a Series C company with $220M in total funding, backed by Goldman Sachs, Bessemer, Y Combinator, Thoma Bravo, and others. Headquartered in San Francisco, TRM operates as a distributed-first company with hubs in Los Angeles, San Francisco, New York, Washington D.C., London, and Singapore. </p><h3></h3><h2><strong>Privacy Policy and Additional Information</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">By submitting your application, you agree to allow TRM Labs to process your personal information in accordance with our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://www.trmlabs.com/policies/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We collect the information you provide (such as your resume, work history, and contact details) solely for the purpose of evaluating your candidacy for current and future roles at TRM.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Because our hiring cycles for certain positions may span 24 to 36 months, we retain your personal information for up to 36 months from the date of your application. After that period, your data is deleted unless a different retention period is required or permitted by law.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you are located in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or another jurisdiction with applicable data protection laws, you have the right to access, correct, or request deletion of your personal data at any time before that period ends. To exercise any of these rights, contact us at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" ---------- style="min-height:1.5em">To notify TRM Labs that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc6e8jRCl2cQwgIzXLpIGQXtwvMQh__TcokvO2toAAkT44A6Q/viewform?usp=dialog">form</a>. No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The use of AI tools of any kind (including but not limited to notetakers, interview assistants, and real-time coaching tools such as Otter.ai, Fireflies, Fathom, Cluey, or similar) during TRM interviews is not permitted without prior approval from TRM. TRM uses its own internal tools for note-taking to ensure a consistent and confidential experience for all candidates. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSevmAzPxWOYm_7kMHb9lEJlX3tpdBeHvvvNWjsI_6xhUfnXjw/viewform?usp=dialog">form</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Recruitment agencies</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">TRM Labs does not accept unsolicited agency resumes. Please do not forward resumes to TRM employees. TRM Labs is not responsible for any fees related to unsolicited resumes and will not pay fees to any third-party agency or company without a signed agreement.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/trm-labs/account-director-private-sector-cee-central-asia-emea-182772","tags":["Go-To-Market"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"EMEA","created_at":1792788026},{"slug":"it-cloud-administrator-munich-292416","company_name":"Munich Electrification","title":"IT Cloud Administrator (f/m/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Munich Electrification</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Munich Electrification is an innovative company founded with the aim of accelerating the transition to electric and connected mobility. We develop innovative electronic control units for electric vehicles and stationary storage systems for our global customers. Our international team is composed of highly motivated and exceptional engineers. As a small and specialized team we are well-aware of the importance of each individual colleague and support and promote each employee according to their abilities and needs. Our office with adjacent prototype and testing lab is located in the heart of Munich at the Heimeranplatz.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is what we stand for:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- <strong>Technological Leadership</strong>: We challenge norms, innovate quickly, and anticipate future needs. We take smart risks and learn from outcomes to stay ahead.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- <strong>Sustainability</strong>: We actively drive change for a sustainable future, aware of our impact and inspiring others to build a better world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">-<strong> Team Culture</strong>: We believe work should be enjoyable, fostering a spirit of inspiration, celebration, and teamwork across the globe.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- <strong>Entrepreneurial Spirit</strong>: We embrace change, think big, and push limits with passion.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Your Role:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your primary mission is to own and evolve our<strong> Digital Ecosystem</strong>, ensuring our cloud-first infrastructure is as innovative and high-performing as our battery technology. You will ensure that our core platforms (<strong>Google Workspace</strong> and the <strong>Atlassian</strong>) function as a seamless, interconnected network that empowers our company. Acting as the vital bridge between business requirements and technical execution, you will master the configuration of existing solutions and be the technical lead for new application/service implementations.<br /><br /><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>SaaS &amp; Cloud Governance</strong>: Act as the Platform Owner for <strong>Google Workspace </strong>and <strong>Atlassian</strong>, managing configurations, security, and permissions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Business Process Evolution</strong>: Work with department heads to translate business needs into scalable digital workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Vendor &amp; Stakeholder Contact</strong>: Coordinate with external consultants and developers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Documentation &amp; Training</strong>: Maintain high-quality documentation of our application landscape and lead training sessions for power users.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Your Profile:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Education</strong>: Degree in Business Informatics, Computer Science, or equivalent professional experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience</strong>: <strong>Min. 3-5 years of experience</strong> as a <strong>Full-time Cloud/IT Administrator</strong>. Proven track record in Application Management, specifically with MDM systems and Cloud/SaaS environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical Expertise:</strong> Good knowledge of <strong>Atlassian </strong>and <strong>Google Workspace</strong> administration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Analytical Mindset</strong>: You enjoy mapping complex business processes into clean, digital solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Communication</strong>: Fluent in English; German is a plus; Ability to explain technical concepts to non-IT stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Optional:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with<strong> AWS</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Google Cloud Identity &amp; SSO integrations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Certification in ITIL</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>SAP Knowledge</strong>: Practical experience with SAP (ByDesign or S/4HANA).<br /><br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Offer &amp; Benefits</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The chance to be part of a highly innovative, agile, and unique team with prestigious customers in the automotive and battery storage sector. You will gain a deeper knowledge around connected &amp; electric vehicle batteries, battery management and electronics development and strive in an exciting work environment</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits (Full-time Employees):</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Trust-based working hours and hybrid work</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Adequate and competitive compensation</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Pension Plan/Bonus</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Free access to the fitness center right next to us or subsidized EGYM Wellpass</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Free snacks, coffee, drinks and lunch (freshly cooked by our chef) every day</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Public transport ticket</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Bike-Leasing via Business Bike</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Experience various inspiring and fun team events</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- ME-branded clothing</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Option to "work from anywhere" (6 weeks/year)</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/munich-electrification/it-cloud-administrator-munich-292416","tags":["Munich Electrification"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1792788019},{"slug":"staff-product-manager-platform-berlin-190170","company_name":"Nelly Solutions","title":"Staff Product Manager - Platform","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a<strong> Staff Product Manager</strong> to take on the hardest problems in the data and integration platform that everything at Nelly runs on: how practice data gets into Nelly from dozens of practice management systems, how partners connect to us, and how that data becomes something every product can depend on. At Staff level, your scope follows the problem, across teams and over time into product-wide questions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The problem space:</strong> Every Nelly product, from documentation to billing to payments, depends on data that lives in a practice's management system. There are dozens of them, each with its own data model and interfaces. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">How many practices we can serve, how much of their work we can automate, and how much they trust the result come down to four questions: can we connect, can we read and write deeply enough, is the data any good once it arrives, and can every product and team inside Nelly easily build on it?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Nelly</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are building the AI-Driven Financial Operating System for European healthcare, solving the biggest challenges for patients and practices. We create what no bank or software platform can handle. Our all-in-one platform transforms chaotic administrative processes into intelligent, automated workflows, from patient care to billing to next-generation payments. Because we truly believe: healthcare should be less about paperwork and more about people.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why? </strong>Because Europe is facing a massive shortage of medical professionals. And if we don't rethink the way practices work, the system won't be able to keep up. With our Series B funding of over €50 million from world-class investors, we are turning our vision into reality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What sets us apart:</strong> We work with the best team, which is why we give everything together every day. We believe in Talent Density, because exceptional people make everyone around them better. At Nelly, we move fast and expect everyone to keep up. Stagnation isn’t an option, which is why we invest heavily in growth. AI is an essential part of how we work at Nelly. We expect you to use it every day and give you everything you need to do so. You get trust and ownership and we expect you to speak up, even when it's uncomfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Joining us, you will:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the strategy, metrics and roadmap for hard data and integration problems, from how data leaves a practice's system, through ingestion and modelling, to the products that rely on it, tied to real practice value and to how Nelly makes money</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape how partners connect to Nelly through our External API, so we can serve practices on any system and open new markets beyond Germany</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define the core data every product relies on: what a patient, an appointment, a treatment plan or an invoice means, who owns it, and how fresh and reliable it is, with GDPR and health-data regulation built in from the start</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make data and integration quality measurable and visible, and move it, because practices feel a silent failure long before we do</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hold an end-to-end model of the platform and be a credible partner to engineering on architecture and trade-offs</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll bring:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Agency. You go after the problems that matter most, including well beyond your immediate scope, rather than waiting for a roadmap to land on your desk</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort in a high-velocity environment. You move fast, make bold but reversible calls, and challenge early and directly, including upward</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Business-outcome orientation. You're genuinely data-driven: you can name the metric each project moves and let evidence, not gut feel, drive prioritisation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical fluency. You reason confidently about APIs, data models, data flows and how systems fit together, and you're a credible partner to senior engineers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You build with AI. You use AI to move faster: prototyping to pressure-test an idea, taking a first pass on the analysis or the spec yourself, shipping the small things directly, so your time goes to judgment and the decisions that move the product</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of product management experience</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Even better if you have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Built and shipped AI products</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Worked on data platforms or data products</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Built B2B SaaS in healthcare or another regulated industry</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional Germa