rcial teams, you will set the principles, guardrails and ways of working that support scalable, long-term commercial performance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your day-to-day:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape cross-market Revenue Management strategy, setting clear commercial principles, policies and decision guardrails.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use market and operational insight to identify structural opportunities to strengthen our pricing power and long-term commercial performance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead cross-functional strategic initiatives and experiments with commercial and Platform teams from concept to delivery, navigating trade-offs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify high-value AI use cases and apply AI tools to improve the Revenue Management team’s efficiency, capacity and quality of output.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Platform to shape the roadmap for new Revenue Management and AI capabilities, translating commercial needs into scalable systems and tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and embed consistent methods, playbooks and operating rhythms that strengthen the Revenue Management function.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a trusted commercial sounding board, bringing Revenue Management insight to decisions and initiatives across the business.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your skillset:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant experience in Revenue Management, pricing strategy or a comparable commercial role, shaping direction across markets, products or customer segments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent commercial judgement, able to navigate ambiguity, challenge assumptions and make well-reasoned trade-offs that support long-term value and growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advanced analytical and experimentation skills, able to set robust measurement approaches and use evidence to inform strategic choices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven ability to lead complex cross-functional programmes, building alignment with commercial and platform stakeholders around shared outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong technical and product awareness, able to translate commercial needs into scalable capability roadmaps and identify high-value applications of AI and automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Credible, influential communication skills, able to turn complex analysis into clear, compelling narratives for senior stakeholders and cross-functional audiences</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Desirable:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Travel-sector or marketplace experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using AI tools to increase team effectiveness and improve commercial decision-making.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with SQL, Looker or comparable analytical tools.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The interview journey:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">TA screening - 30 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1st stage with Hiring Manager - 45 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2nd stage with key stakeholders including a task to present, in office - 1.5 hours</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final stage with Chief Data Officer - 30 mins</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/loveholidays/lead-pricing-revenue-manager-london-201931","tags":["Revenue & International"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792798814},{"slug":"senior-crm-executive-london-310094","company_name":"loveholidays","title":"Senior CRM Executive","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why loveholidays?</strong><br />At loveholidays - <strong>we trailblaze together</strong>. We’re on a mission to open the world to everyone, giving our customers’ unlimited choice, unmatched ease and unmissable value for their next getaway. Our team is the driving force behind our role as our customers’ personal holiday expert - the smart way to get away.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re using progressive tech to <strong>drive cutting-edge innovation</strong> and open the world to everyone. Within our <em>Commercial and Support teams</em>, you'll find a place to <strong>accelerate your growth</strong> by actively seeking learning opportunities and carving your own path. You'll <strong>create impact for our future</strong> by owning projects and shaping the business strategy to reach shared goals, all within our <strong>enhanced international community</strong> of collaborative and passionate teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>The impact you’ll have:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our Senior CRM Executive, you will play a key role in delivering and improving CRM campaigns and customer journeys across our channels. You’ll be close to the detail of campaign build, journey optimisation and performance, with the opportunity to grow your ownership over time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll work closely with the CRM Manager, Head of CRM and wider Marketing, Product and Engineering teams to turn agreed customer opportunities and briefs into well-executed campaigns and journeys. You’ll help move us away from legacy campaign cycles by building reliable, increasingly automated lifecycle activity. We are looking for a thoughtful, high-velocity operator who can turn clear direction into accurate live journeys.<br /><br /><br /><strong>Your day-to-day:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll build and maintain multi-channel automated journeys using branching logic, API triggers, and real-time data, working from agreed briefs and priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify manual bottlenecks and support the implementation of AI-assisted workflows, using tools like n8n and Claude (training will be provided).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use Braze to identify optimisation opportunities within your journeys and help make delivery faster, more accurate, and more consistent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide hands-on campaign support to the wider team in deploying campaigns. You’ll ensure accurate execution through rigorous, increasingly automated QA processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work collaboratively with Marketing, Product and Engineering to deliver agreed workstreams and help create a frictionless experience from search to rebooking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor the performance of your campaigns and journeys. You’ll be comfortable using Looker to maintain reports, monitor health metrics, and surface actionable insights that support optimisation.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Your skillset:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a reliable operator who takes ownership of your assigned campaigns and journeys from brief through deployment. You ask the right questions, flag risks early, and deliver with consistency and precision.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can move from a clear brief to deployment rapidly, maintaining high standards and following agreed processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are naturally curious and look for practical ways to improve processes, reduce manual tasks, and make delivery more efficient.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have experience with Looker, Tableau, or SQL, and BQ and confidence using data to monitor performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with Braze or similar. You should be comfortable with Liquid logic, audience segmentation and personalisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are comfortable working with data models and propensity scores to support relevant segmentation and measure campaign impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to work well across Marketing, Product, and Engineering teams, taking direction and communicating clearly to keep delivery on track.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Desirable:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting CRM activity across multiple international markets, including handling localisation, consent frameworks, and currency differences within automated journeys</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with n8n or similar workflow automation tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience writing Liquid logic for content personalisation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to AI-assisted workflows or agentic tooling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in travel, marketplace, or another high-frequency transactional category<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>The interview journey:</strong></p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meeting with a member of the Talent Acquisition team - 20 minutes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Virtual Interview with Hiring Manager</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final Stage interview in office presenting pre-determined task and a meeting a few stakeholders - 1 hour 30 mins <br /></p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Perks of joining us:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company pension contributions at 5%.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Individualised training budget for you to learn on the job and level yourself up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discounted holidays for you, your family and friends.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days of holidays per annum (plus 8 public holidays) increases by 1 day for every second year of service, up to a maximum 30 days per annum.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to buy and sell annual leave.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cycle to work scheme, season ticket loan and eye care vouchers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At loveholidays, we focus on developing an inclusive culture and environment that encourages personal growth and collective success. Each individual offers unique perspectives and ideas that increase the diversity and effectiveness of our teams. And we value the insight and potential you could bring on our continued journey.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/loveholidays/senior-crm-executive-london-310094","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792798814},{"slug":"demand-generation-manager-manchester-260695","company_name":"Ryftpay","title":"Demand Generation Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Ryft</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ryft is a regulated payment facilitator and authorised payment institution building the infrastructure layer for modern commerce platforms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We enable marketplaces, SaaS platforms and multi-party ecosystems to embed and monetise payments natively. Our technology handles onboarding, compliance, orchestration, split payments and revenue sharing, allowing our partners to focus on growth while we manage complexity.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are now entering the next phase of scale, expanding into new verticals and building a category-defining embedded payments platform.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a growing, high-performing company led by serial founders and backed by exceptional investors. We're looking for a Demand Generation Manager to help drive our marketing activities - someone who fits the T shaped marketing profile: a working knowledge across marketing, with real depth in at least one or two disciplines.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your responsibilities will include:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Executing and helping shape the demand generation plan across a broad mix of channels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Planning and running cross-functional activities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Helping build and execute ABM campaigns </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintaining a clear attribution picture so we know what's actually driving pipeline from their activities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building and improving marketing automation workflows to support lead flow, nurture, and sales handoff</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working closely with sales to align activity with pipeline targets and refine ICP targeting</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for someone who is analytical and is comfortable working across a broad remit.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Must-haves</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">4-6 years in marketing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">B2B experience is mandatory, ideally in fintech</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">T-shaped profile: hands-on working knowledge across a broad mix of marketing channels, with proven depth in at least one</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of running campaigns with clear, commercial results</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working with Hubspot, Clay and LinkedIn Ads</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to work autonomously and prioritise across multiple concurrent workstreams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable briefing and directing others (freelancers, internal stakeholders)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Happy to run owned and third-party events</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building marketing automation workflows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a scale-up environment, building processes rather than inheriting them</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Culture</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We give people the tools and the support to execute at their best. No politics, no unnecessary meetings, no painfully complex sign-off processes. If that resonates, you'll fit right in.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/ryftpay/demand-generation-manager-manchester-260695","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Manchester","created_at":1792798814},{"slug":"revenue-operations-manager-london-423677","company_name":"Healthtech 1","title":"Revenue Operations Manager","description":"<h1><strong>We're unlocking access to the NHS, because healthcare is not truly free until it's truly accessible 💙</strong></h1><div><div style="left:0px;width:100%;height:0px;position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%"><iframe src="https://embedded-media.ashbyhq.com/embed/f9fa51ed-2e44-43fa-9869-fd67aaa703ac/2deb0a62-4225-4f9f-a607-44b7b30c7cbf" style="top:0px;left:0px;width:100%;height:100%;position:absolute;border:0px" allowfullscreen="true" scrolling="no" allow="encrypted-media *; picture-in-picture *;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation"></iframe></div></div><p style="min-height:1.5em">The world’s best healthcare, for free. It's not a new idea, it's called the NHS. But the largest healthcare provider is fundamentally broken. Patient satisfaction is at an all time low, and the biggest reason cited is lack of access. So we’re on a mission to fix it with technology that actually works.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're building the front door of UK healthcare, creating a future where one billion NHS appointments are transparent and instantly bookable, and patients are guided to the right service first time using AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're developing critical national infrastructure. Today, 26% of GP practices in England use our patient registration software, while one in five GP practices in London use <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://bookable.health/?utm_source=ashby">Bookable</a> Search to help new patients find and book appointments seamlessly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our latest product, Bookable Navigator, extends this vision by automatically booking appointments for existing patients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We operate from within a working GP practice in East London 🏥 We're backed by Y Combinator, Innovate UK and the NHS Clinical Entrepreneur Programme, and were previously ranked the 8th fastest-growing startup in the UK and 33rd fastest-growing in Europe 🚀</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>⛩️ Our Principles </h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exciting challenges lie ahead. Guided by our principles, we’ll meet these challenges with a thoughtful and caring approach. These principles drive everything we do at Healthtech-1:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💙 Care deeply</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏋️‍♀️ Work hard</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤝 Be your word</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💬 Trust in radical truth and transparency</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> 🚀 Do your life's best work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🥳 Find the fun</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em">Read more about our principles and our "why" in the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://link.ht1.uk/handbook">Healthtech-1 Handbook</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>🎯 Goal expectations</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our <strong>Revenue Operations Manager</strong>, you’ll own the tooling and data that let’s Healthtech-1 scale across the NHS. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll work closely across the GTM teams, deploy internal tooling with AI, turn Attio into our source of truth, and build an intelligent GTM motion on top.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an IC role, not a people management role. One week you might be rolling your sleeves up with the growth team, to be one or two steps ahead in identifying what the team need to hit their targets, and building internal tooling with AI to support the team. The next week you might be deep in the data, bringing company-wide data sources together to aide growth strategy planning e.g. identifying high demand areas in our marketplace, where we need to increase supply.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Objective 1: Keep systems and data running at a high standard</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will own and maintain Attio (our CRM), including its infrastructure, workflows and data hygiene across accounts and products. You will also own all our GTM tooling (e.g. Aircall, Calendly, Granola) and keep them running and improving. You will build a lot of tooling yourself using AI (e.g. dashboard, maps). You will run practice enrichment and data scraping pipelines so our data on customers stays current and usable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Objective 2: Give the team and leadership clear visibility</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will build and maintain dashboards tracking company growth, cycle targets and product adoption. You will own reporting on practice numbers and growth trends. You will maintain tracking so leadership always has clear visibility on where deals are at.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Objective 3: Enable the growth team to sell more</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Growth team are your customer. You will build and maintain quality lead lists for AEs. You will support AEs with operational queries, targets and tooling. You will help new growth hires ramp faster through better tooling and playbooks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Objective 4: Drive operational improvement</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will find and build automations and workflow improvements that save the team time. You will spot friction in how the growth team operates and fix it. You will actively look for ways to help the team drive more revenue.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>⚠️ This role is not for everyone</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a high-ownership, high-expectation role. You'll be working in a fast-moving healthtech environment where accuracy, speed, and proactivity all matter at the same time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You probably won't enjoy this role if you:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prefer to be told what to do over figuring out what to do</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Treat ops as a support function rather than a growth lever</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aren't comfortable getting your hands dirty with data</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are content to maintain the status quo rather than improve it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have never built things with AI</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will enjoy this role if you like owning systems end-to-end, building and deploying things with AI, and making the people around you more effective.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>👍 Required experience</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years in a revenue operations role in an early-stage startup, where you've owned systems, data and process improvement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Attio (or similar CRMs like HubSpot, Salesforce)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>✅ Must-have traits</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Great with AI</strong> - you know how to leverage AI well, whilst thoroughly checking accuracy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Detail oriented</strong> - you’re obsessed with the detail and CRM being the source of truth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Love data</strong> - you can build dashboards, spot trends, and make data useful for decision-making</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proactive problem solver</strong> - you don't wait for someone to flag a problem; you find it and fix it end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bias to action</strong> - you ship improvements quickly rather than over-planning</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team player</strong> - low ego, approachable and feedback-oriented; you get a kick from seeing the impact your work has on unlocking the sales team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clear communicator</strong> - you keep stakeholders informed without being chased</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>💙 Desired traits</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with data scraping, enrichment tools and light automation (e.g. Zapier, Make, scripts)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building dashboards and reports (e.g. Metabase, Looker, Google Sheets)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with sales tooling (Calendly, Aircall, or equivalents)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience writing operational playbooks or onboarding materials</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>😊 The hiring process (4 stages)</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">👋 Intro chat - with our Talent Partner, to learn more about each other</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">📝 Take home task - complete a short task</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💼 An in-office work trial - work with the growth team on a real problem [1 day, fully paid]</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">⛩️ Principles interview - with a Founder, to understand that our values align</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎉 Offer!</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>💙 A bit about us</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">💙 We’re all NHS staff. We’re inside-outsiders. Trusted with one of the biggest datasets in the world. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏥 Our office is within a GP practice. This is our unfair advantage. Got a question? Pop down the corridor. Want to learn how your work affects real patients? Pop downstairs to reception. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💪🏼 4 days in the office and 1 day WFH (for most roles). We highly prioritise in-person communication and prefer candidates who want to work 4+ days a week in the office. Our anchor days are Mon, Tues, Thurs and Fri. Homemade breakfast and lunch are on the house every day when you're in the office, ensuring you're fuelled for success!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌀 We work in growth cycles. Every 8 weeks we do the same set of activities. 1 week outside of Business-as-Usual to research, strategise, plan our work. 7 weeks to knuckle down and deliver it. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤝 We’re highly collaborative. One of the benefits of a high trust team is we often work autonomously, but as a team we’re very collaborative by nature. Two heads are often better than one, and we frequently lean on each other to solve problems together. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤜🏽 We’re backed by industry leaders. We’re on the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://DigitalHealth.London">DigitalHealth.London</a> Accelerator, backed by the NHS Clinical Entrepreneur Program, winners of the London Business School Healthtech Challenge, Innovate UK, and Y Combinator (S23).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>🚀 An opportunity for real upside</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">💉 Paid volunteer days. We offer an additional 2 paid days off per year where you can give back to your mission of choice.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎢 Every 8 weeks we take a day off to socialise as a team. In the past we’ve hiked box hill, raved at All Points East and spent one rainy day at Thorpe park. This works out as 6 working days a year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">📚 Learning budget of £250 annually and time off to spend it - we care about this; this is flexible and based on need but everyone will receive a yearly allocation towards their continual growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🍽️ Homemade breakfast and lunch are on the house when you're in the office, ensuring you're fuelled for success!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🥡 Team takeaways every Monday night</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🥗 Health and fitness budget of £60 per month - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/Health-and-fitness-bc845193dccd44cda9cdcd1f8ba6305e?pvs=21">see more here</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🧘‍♂️ An additional 7 days of paid leave is available if you want to take time to learn how to meditate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💫 Tooling; You’ll have your choice of operating systems and any additional tools you need to do your best work (e.g. keyboard, additional monitors, mouse etc). If you’re on our Engineering teams you’ll receive the latest MacBook Pro and our Growth &amp; Ops teams receives a MacBook Air.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🩺 We know health and family come first which is why we have a generous sick leave policy with additional days that can be taken for mental health leave.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✈️ We prioritise time outside of work to bond, once a year we’ll holiday together! Destination chosen by popular vote. In 2025, we spent 8 days in a surf camp in France!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">👎 No private medical insurance, because we believe in the NHS and we are here to improve it!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🐥 Parental leave: Post passing probation it is: statutory - 6 weeks 90% pay then, SMP for 33 weeks; if you've been an employee for a year: 12 weeks 100% pay then, SMP for 27 weeks; and if you have been here for 2 years: 18 weeks 100% pay then, SMP for 21 weeks. This will improve over time. We also include up to £9,000 of childcare contribution for primary caregivers to support a five-day return where possible.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">👪 Fertility leave. We understand how difficult a fertility journey can be. This is why we give an extra 5 days off per year if you or your partner are going through fertility treatment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🐖 Pension - We operate a standard 3% employer contribution and employees auto-contribute 5% of their salary. We use Nest as our provider.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏡 Local living benefit - A one-off benefit to support living closer to the office: £5,000 if you live within a 30-min