&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Salary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Annual salary is benchmarked to role scope and relevant experience. Most offers land between £65,000 and £145,000 made up of a base salary plus a technical allowance (take-home salary = base + technical allowance). An additional 28.97% employer pension contribution is paid on the base salary.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;This role sits outside of the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ddat-capability-framework.service.gov.uk/&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;DDaT pay framework&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;given the scope of this role requires in depth technical&amp;nbsp;expertise&amp;nbsp;in frontier AI safety,&amp;nbsp;robustness&amp;nbsp;and advanced AI architectures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The full range of salaries are available below:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level 3:&lt;/strong&gt; £65,000–£75,000 (Base £40,850 + Technical Allowance £24,150–£34,150)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level 4:&lt;/strong&gt; £85,000–£95,000 (Base £48,540 + Technical Allowance £36,460–£46,460)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level 5:&lt;/strong&gt; £105,000–£115,000 (Base £63,165 + Technical Allowance £41,835–£51,835)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level 6:&lt;/strong&gt; £125,000–£135,000 (Base £76,475 + Technical Allowance £48,525–£58,525)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level 7:&lt;/strong&gt; £145,000 (Base £76,475 + Technical Allowance £68,525)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Additional Information&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_nullclass&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use of AI in Applications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Artificial Intelligence can be a useful tool to support your application, however, all examples and statements provided must be truthful, factually accurate and taken directly from your own experience. Where plagiarism has been identified (presenting the ideas and experiences of others, or generated by artificial intelligence, as your own) applications may be withdrawn and internal candidates may be subject to disciplinary action. Please see our&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://eur02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.civil-service-careers.gov.uk%2Fartificial-intelligence-and-recruitment%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7CLynn.Tan%40dsit.gov.uk%7Ccf5d753b7f19427afc8f08de4c307014%7Ccbac700502c143ebb497e6492d1b2dd8%7C0%7C0%7C639031968075235036%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=jCrYoy62YfXN%2FLIB%2FhtHxdLGbCOgropbkZXDyQsUMC4%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;02db05e7-03ca-4ca6-bcd9-73ff8bf258f2&quot; data-auth=&quot;NotApplicable&quot; data-linkindex=&quot;1&quot;&gt;candidate guidance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;for more information on appropriate and inappropriate use.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use of AI tools in recruitment&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We may use AI tools to help our hiring team review applications, for example by summarising application materials and helping us prioritise them against the published criteria. We do not use AI tools to find information about you from other sources, including online.&amp;nbsp;People make every decision. We do not make solely automated decisions about candidates. Find out more, including your rights, in our recruitment privacy notice: https://www.aisi.gov.uk/careers/privacy-policy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internal Fraud Database&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;The Internal Fraud function of the Fraud, Error, Debt and Grants Function at the Cabinet Office processes details of civil servants who have been dismissed for committing internal fraud, or who would have been dismissed had they not resigned. The Cabinet Office receives the details from participating government organisations of civil servants who have been dismissed, or who would have been dismissed had they not resigned, for internal fraud. In instances such as this, civil servants are then banned for 5 years from further employment in the civil service. The Cabinet Office then processes this data and discloses a limited dataset back to DLUHC as a participating government organisations. DLUHC then carry out the pre employment checks so as to detect instances where known fraudsters are attempting to reapply for roles in the civil service. In this way, the policy is ensured and the repetition of internal fraud is prevented.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;For more information please see -&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/internal-fraud-register-privacy-notice/internal-fraud-register-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Internal Fraud Register.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Security&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Successful candidates must undergo a criminal record check and get&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/government-baseline-personnel-security-standard&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/government-baseline-personnel-security-standard&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;baseline personnel security standard (BPSS)&amp;nbsp;clearance&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;before they can be appointed. Additionally, there is a strong preference for eligibility for&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/national-security-vetting-advice-for-people-who-are-being-vetted&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/national-security-vetting-advice-for-people-who-are-being-vetted&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;counter-terrorist check (CTC)&amp;nbsp;clearance&lt;/a&gt;. Some roles may require higher levels of clearance, and we will state this by exception in the job advertisement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/vetting-explained-and-our-vetting-charter/the-vetting-charter&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/vetting-explained-and-our-vetting-charter/the-vetting-charter&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;See our vetting charter here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Nationality requirements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;We may be able to offer roles to applicant from &lt;strong&gt;any nationality or background&lt;/strong&gt;. As such we encourage you to apply even if you do not meet the standard &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/nationality-rules&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;nationality requirements (opens in a new window).&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Working for the Civil Service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field_value&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://civilservicecommission.independent.gov.uk/code/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Civil Service Code (opens in a new window)&lt;/a&gt; sets out the standards of behaviour expected of civil servants.&amp;nbsp;The Civil Service embraces diversity and promotes equal opportunities. As such, we run a Disability Confident Scheme (DCS) for candidates with disabilities who meet the minimum selection criteria.&amp;nbsp;The Civil Service also offers a Redeployment Interview Scheme to civil servants who are at risk of redundancy, and who meet the minimum requirements for the advertised vacancy.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field_value&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;The Civil Service is committed to attract, retain and invest in talent wherever it is found. To learn more please see the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/civil-service-people-plan-2024-2027/civil-service-people-plan-2024-2027-html&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Civil Service People Plan (opens in a new window)&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/civil-service-diversity-and-inclusion-strategy-2022-to-2025&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Civil Service Diversity and Inclusion Strategy (opens in a new window)&lt;/a&gt;. As part of the application process, we monitor statistics on D&amp;amp;I. You can see how we process this data here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/government-digital-service-recruitment-privacy-notice/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment privacy notice - GOV.UK&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/aisi/alignment-red-team-research-engineer-research-scientist-london-265860","tags":["Red Team"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792788919},{"slug":"senior-risk-assurance-manager-eu-uk-london-7432","company_name":"Trustly","title":"Senior Risk & Assurance Manager EU/UK","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHO WE ARE</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Trustly, we're building a smarter, faster, and more secure financial future by revolutionizing the world of payments. As a global leader in Open Banking Payments, we are establishing Pay by Bank as the new standard at checkout, providing unparalleled freedom, speed, and ease to millions of consumers and merchants worldwide.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Ambition: To build the world’s most disruptive payment network and redefine what the payment experience should feel like.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Trustly is a global team of innovators, collaborators, and doers. If you are driven by a strong sense of purpose and thrive in a dynamic, entrepreneurial, and high-growth environment, join us and be part of a team that’s transforming the way the world pays.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ABOUT THE ROLE</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are building a dedicated Risk and Compliance Assurance function in the Second Line of Defence, and we are seeking a Senior Risk and Assurance Manager to own a single view of the second-line risk and control environment across Trustly's EU and UK regulated entities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the Senior Risk and Assurance Manager, you will lead entity-level assurance and second-line risk oversight for Trustly’s EU and UK regulated entities, supported by the Global Enterprise Risk Management framework. This role will be part of a wider community of risk and assurance managers, which will also cover specific compliance domains (such as Financial Crimes Prevention, Safeguarding, Consumer Protection, ICT and Resilience).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The focus of this role is the regulated entities in the UK and EU. You will confirm that domain testing reflects local requirements and local regulator expectations, and report findings to the entity Boards. You will serve as the primary point of contact for UK and EU regulators on risk and assurance matters.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is suited to a seasoned assurance, compliance, and/or second-line risk professional with experience in regulated financial/payment institutions, ideally with experience of engaging with regulators.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage assurance at an entity level for Trustly’s EU and UK regulated entities, and be responsible for risk in these entities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own a single view of the second-line control and risk environment across Trustly's EU and UK regulated entities, and contribute to standardised reporting including Key Risk Indicators and unified tracking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confirm the local regulatory applicability of domain testing scope and methodology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the assurance opinion, reporting of findings, and the risk view to each entity Board and local management team, and support what the entity Compliance lead attests to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to the annual assurance planning through active engagement in an assurance forum, jointly reviewing and signing off scope with the relevant domain assurance managers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as a primary point of contact toward the relevant EU and UK regulators/supervisors on risk and assurance matters, representing the function confidently and credibly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support Internal Audit's reliance assessment by maintaining a transparent, evidenced audit trail per test, and document any risk-accepted changes to testing cadence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHO YOU ARE</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years experience as a compliance assurance and/or second-line risk manager</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payments sector experience preferred</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience engaging with EU and/or UK financial supervisory authorities is desired</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A confident and articulate approach, demonstrating an ability to represent the risk and assurance function credibly and build productive relationships across business teams, and to advise and collaborate with stakeholders at various levels, including senior management and Board members.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sound understanding of the EU and UK regulatory landscape relevant to payment institutions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to lead end-to-end assurance reviews; planning, scoping, reporting and issue validation, including knowledge of control testing methodologies, sampling, issue rating, and evidence standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A firm grasp of the three-lines model and the independence boundary between second and third line, with the judgement to keep assurance independent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High attention to detail in the preparation of control findings and management-level documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to clearly explain complex concepts and present to senior leadership, Boards, and regulators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to work flexibly to collaborate with team members across different time zones.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>WHAT WE OFFER</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Trustly, you will have the chance to solve meaningful challenges alongside some of the brightest minds in FinTech. Together, we are shaping the future of payments in an environment that celebrates curiosity, collaboration, and innovation. You will be challenged and empowered to grow, making a real impact every step of the way.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our team is as diverse as the global footprint we serve. At Trustly, we foster a workplace where everyone feels they belong—a place where teamwork thrives, ideas flourish, and we never forget to have fun along the way. We are proud and committed to being an Equal Opportunity Employer and believe an open and inclusive environment enables people to do their best work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Fantastic Benefits (varies by location)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌴 <strong>20 to 30 days of holiday</strong> to support a healthy work-life balance</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🥳 <strong>Monthly team outing allowance</strong> to enjoy social events with your colleagues</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">👶 <strong>Parental leave top-up </strong>additional support for new parents</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">☕ <strong>On-site perks </strong>to make your workday smoother</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💚 <strong>Well being support</strong> our health allowance covers gym memberships, massages, and much more to help you feel your best</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>PLUS</strong> additional benefits designed to enhance your work-life experience!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape Your Role and Make an Impact</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join a dynamic environment where you can take ownership, drive change, and continuously embrace new challenges. We’re looking for dedicated and highly motivated individuals who thrive in a fast-paced environment and enjoy collaborating across different areas of the organisation.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/trustly/senior-risk-assurance-manager-eu-uk-london-7432","tags":["Compliance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792788019},{"slug":"experience-operations-london-221275","company_name":"Scarlet","title":"Experience Operations","description":"<h2><strong>We pull medical technology from the future to solve human health.</strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scarlet is authorised to assess and certify medical devices. We combine clinical, technical and regulatory expertise with AI agents and software so rigorous certification can keep pace with product development at the world’s most ambitious technology companies, without lowering the safety bar.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our customers have cut a year or more from their certification timelines for new AI-enabled medical devices and shortened product-update cycles from months to weeks. You’ll join a team building the infrastructure that makes these outcomes repeatable at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who you are</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have spent at least 3 years organising events, exceptional hospitality experiences, or in an operations role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You love problem solving and are fascinated by how to make an events engine hum - from venue sourcing to invite workflows to guest experience and more</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a deep passion for IRL experiences and you’re excited to enable the impact of Scarlet’s events and community to grow exponentially across the world</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have outstanding organisational skills, care about clean data and processes, use AI agents in your work, and you also like to get hands-on</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You approach problems from first principles and adhere to MECE (Mutually Exclusive, Collectively Exhaustive) principles</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Desirable</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have experience building automations within CRMs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've worked in a start-up environment with high ownership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've built event processes, playbooks, or systems that support growth</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>What the job involves</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe in the impact of premium, IRL experiences. We organise 10+ of these per month across the world, and this will soon be 30+. We’re looking for someone to join our Growth team, working closely with our Experience Lead, to develop and scale the systems and processes needed to expand our world-class in-person events globally.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with our Experience Lead to organise premium experiences for customers, sales prospects, media, and other industry stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use agents and work hands-on to build and optimise the system(s) that scale our IRL events and community</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain event playbooks to ensure consistent, world-class delivery as we scale</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify opportunities for automation while preserving a high-touch, hyper-hospitable guest experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Book incredible venues, manage guest logistics, and help produce attendee-delighting events</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create thoughtful pre-event workflows that scale but remain personal</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Craft tools to find exceptional event spaces in any city</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with Sales teammates to design systems that find the right guests, manage invitations, track attendance, and surface important attendee insights</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The interview process</strong></p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Intro call with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/danlevy1/">Dan</a> - 20 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interview call with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/emilyotterbeck/">Emily</a> - 30 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical interviews with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/alice-morris-25b872106/">Alice</a> &amp; <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/danlevy1/">Dan</a> - 2x1 hour</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Culture and values interview with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/james-dewar-78758992/?originalSubdomain=uk">James</a> &amp; <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jamie-cox-01458b3a/?originalSubdomain=uk">Jamie</a> - 2x30 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Referencing &amp; offer</p></li></ol><hr><p>Compensation: £60K – £70K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • £60K – £70K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/scarlet/experience-operations-london-221275","tags":["Growth"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"UK - London Office","created_at":1792788019},{"slug":"product-manager-london-319520","company_name":"Scarlet","title":"Product Manager","description":"<h2><strong>We pull medical technology from the future to solve human health.</strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scarlet is authorised to assess and certify medical devices. We combine clinical, technical and regulatory expertise with AI agents and software so rigorous certification can keep pace with product development at the world’s most ambitious technology companies, without lowering the safety bar.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our customers have cut a year or more from their certification timelines for new AI-enabled medical devices and shortened product-update cycles from months to weeks. You’ll join a team building the infrastructure that makes these outcomes repeatable at scale.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Product Manager at Scarlet, you will own a meaningful product area end to end. You will develop a deep understanding of the people and problems within it, set a clear direction, decide what matters most, and work with product design and engineering to deliver measurable improvements.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will sit close to regulatory experts, account managers and customers in our London office. Their expertise will give you rich signals, but not a ready-made roadmap. Your job is to turn those signals into a coherent product strategy, make trade-offs openly and ensure what we build improves both the quality and speed of certification.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will have substantial autonomy. We will trust you to form a point of view, test it against evidence and change course when the evidence changes.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the strategy, roadmap and outcomes for a product area, from discovery and definition through launch, adoption and iteration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with product design, engineering and regulatory experts to turn complex requirements into clear, trustworthy workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spend time with customers and internal users to understand their work, observe friction and distinguish underlying problems from requested features.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prioritise across customer value, regulatory rigour, operational efficiency, technical constraints and Scarlet’s company goals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the team aligned on the problem, the intended outcome and the trade-offs behind each decision.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate product direction, decisions, progress and learning clearly across Scarlet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help improve how Scarlet practises product management as the team grows.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Required qualifications</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evidence of owning and shipping complex products from discovery through delivery and iteration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong product judgement, including examples of difficult prioritisation choices made under real constraints.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enough technical fluency to work effectively with engineers on systems, data, APIs and the trade-offs of AI-enabled products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear, precise written and verbal communication, including the ability to explain complex decisions to different audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort working in ambiguity, taking responsibility and updating your view when new evidence appears.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High standards for product quality, reliability and trust.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Preferred qualifications</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in health technology, enterprise software, vertical SaaS or another regulated industry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building products for complex, multi-stakeholder or expert-led workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with AI-enabled products, including evaluation, failure modes and appropriate guardrails.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in an early-stage or fast-growing company where product practices were still being formed.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Interview process</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We typically collapse steps 3 to 5 into one in-person session.</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Intro chat</strong> with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/johnnytreasure/">Johnny</a> - 30 minutes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Engineering and design chats</strong> with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/niclaslovenilsson/">Niclas</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https: