&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;5364&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/quince/senior-category-manager-home-eu-london-499479","tags":["International"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792778118},{"slug":"product-manager-london-261454","company_name":"Nexcade","title":"Product Manager","description":"<h1>About us</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">People assume the supply chain is an automated, algorithmic system. In reality, hundred of thousands of operators acting as the glue between organisations and systems, doing work the world depends on, with tools that have barely changed in decades and spending hours a day on email. Nexcade is building the agentic operating system for those people, transforming the way people communicate and optimise the $1T spend on logistics every year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our agents are live in production with leading global Freight Forwarders, pricing millions in freight every week, and we are rapidly expanding the platform to touch every part of the logistics lifecycle.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our founders, Dan and Tasho, spent years at Sedna and Palantir working with supply chain companies on problems like this one. We have raised $8.5M to make this a reality from top VCs and angels who backed or founded Synthesia, n8n and other world-class companies.</p><h1>How we work</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everybody builds, founders included. The whole company is technical and runs on coding agents. You will not be asked to write production software, but you will use agents for discovery synthesis, specs, prototypes and data analysis rather than doing them by hand.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Closely with customers and design partners, so what we ship changes how they operate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At pace. Fast cycles and quick iterations, on the product and on how we work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">End to end. If you see something broken or missing, you have the freedom (and the responsibility) to fix it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">In person, in London. We value synchronous communication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Debate rigorously, decide quickly, execute relentlessly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enjoy the journey. Hard problems, good colleagues.</p></li></ul><h1>The role</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building the AI platform freight forwarders rely on. We started with quoting and are expanding across the shipment lifecycle. As Product Lead, you will be central to that expansion, helping decide where we focus and turning those decisions into products customers depend on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own product outcomes:</strong> Own the roadmap, priorities and performance of specific products, from defining the customer problem through launch, rollout and adoption. Partner with the founders on overall product direction and strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build from customer insight:</strong> Work closely with freight forwarders across commercial and operational roles. Understand how they work, identify the problems customers share and build products for those needs rather than one-off solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Prototype and build:</strong> Turn ideas into working prototypes and early product versions, using AI tools and code to test them with customers. Work hands-on with engineering to take promising ideas into production, not just write specs and hand them over.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive product expansion:</strong> Build a clear view of the market, including where we win, where we do not compete and why customers choose us. Use that understanding to identify the next workflows Nexcade should enter and turn them into products that grow revenue.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Raise the standard of product thinking:</strong> Define success measures, test assumptions and examine accuracy, edge cases and second-order effects before scaling. Write clear specs and decision documents, including a written recommendation on the hard calls.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the product operating system:</strong> Establish a clear planning and decision-making cadence without adding bureaucracy. Make sure product meetings are well prepared, teams have the context they need and decisions translate into shipped work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make product and platform trade-offs:</strong> Work closely with engineering to decide when to invest in shared capabilities and when a faster, product-specific approach is right.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What we look for</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong product judgement:</strong> You have owned meaningful product work in a complex B2B product and can show how your decisions changed customer behaviour or business results. You define success clearly and test assumptions, accuracy and edge cases before scaling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product taste:</strong> You can turn complex workflows into products that feel simple, coherent and trustworthy. You care about the details that make people choose to use them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical fluency:</strong> You work effectively with strong engineers, understand trade-offs across architecture, AI, data and integrations and bring the customer and product perspective to choices about speed, quality and reuse.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Excellent judgement:</strong> You get beyond what customers ask for to understand how their work really happens and distinguish repeatable needs from bespoke requests. You use customer and market insight to make product choices that drive adoption, expansion and revenue.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High agency and directness:</strong> You take ownership, hold a high bar and disagree openly and constructively. You are comfortable with ambiguity, fast iteration and changing priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Obsess over the problem:</strong> You are drawn to complex, messy problems in industries the economy depends on and want to understand how the people and systems behind them really work. Industry experience is a bonus, but not required.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Why join</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The biggest product choices are still ahead: how deep we go, where we expand and how everything fits together. Our product is already live with leading freight forwarders and this role will shape what comes next. You will build AI for the work that keeps global trade moving, alongside a team from Palantir, Raft, Faculty, UnlikelyAI and Oxford. You will get meaningful equity in the company you help build.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/nexcade/product-manager-london-261454","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792777219},{"slug":"associate-implementation-consultant-london-350623","company_name":"Snyk","title":"Associate Implementation Consultant","description":"<h2><strong>Unleash AI Innovators, Securely</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Software is being rewritten in real time. AI agents are starting to write more code than humans do, at a speed no security team has ever had to match, and that single shift is opening up the biggest opportunity our industry has seen in a decade. We're not bracing for it, we're building the company that owns it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Snyk is building the next generation security platform where security isn't a set of tools people operate.  It's a team of security agents working alongside your engineers, finding, fixing, and governing risk at the speed software is now built. These agents work alongside both the company build and the agents they adopt. Security stops being a queue of work waiting for people, and becomes a coordinated workforce companies direct and trust.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Job Summary</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Snyk is hiring an Associate Implementation Consultant to help enterprise customers get started with the Snyk platform after the sale. You will support and deliver onboarding engagements, working with customer development and security teams to configure Snyk across their SDLC, CI/CD pipelines, and cloud infrastructure. This is an early-career role for someone with a technical foundation who wants to build a career in customer-facing application security, with hands-on work from your first weeks and structured coaching from experienced consultants along the way.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Customer Solutions team owns the technical success of Snyk's customers after the deal closes, from first onboarding session through full platform adoption. Implementation Consultants work alongside Technical Success, Support, Sales, and Product to turn a customer's security goals into a deployed, measurable program. As Snyk's install base continues to grow, this team is expanding to keep delivering a world-class onboarding experience at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver onboarding engagements for customers with well-defined requirements, following Snyk's onboarding methodology from kick-off through closure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support senior consultants on larger and more complex implementations, taking ownership of defined workstreams and learning how enterprise rollouts are planned and run.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Configure and integrate the Snyk platform with customer source control, CI/CD, container, and cloud environments, working from documented procedures and escalating questions early.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join customer kick-offs, working sessions, and status reviews, and keep customer contacts informed on progress and next steps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Answer customer questions about how Snyk works, and bring in senior consultants, Support, or Product when an issue needs deeper expertise.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep accurate project plans, notes, and handoff documentation so every engagement is easy for others to pick up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use Snyk's onboarding playbooks and templates, and suggest improvements when you find gaps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Troubleshoot common integration and configuration issues, and document what you learn for the rest of the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help customer teams understand developer-first security practices so they keep using Snyk after onboarding ends.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build your skills through regular coaching, shadowing, and Snyk's technical training and certification programs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1+ years in technical consulting, professional services, technical support, or another customer-facing technical role, or equivalent hands-on experience such as an internship or relevant projects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Foundational knowledge of the SDLC and modern DevOps practices, and curiosity about where security fits into both.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with CI/CD and DevOps tooling (for example Jenkins, GitHub Actions, GitLab, Azure DevOps, Kubernetes), with the motivation to go deeper.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to manage your own tasks and deadlines across more than one customer project, with support from your team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to explain technical topics clearly to developers and other technical contacts, in writing and in conversation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine interest in application security and belief that a developer-first approach is the right way to solve it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative, customer-first approach and a willingness to ask questions, take feedback, and learn quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working fluency with AI-assisted tools (Claude, Gemini, or similar) and comfort with how AI-generated code is changing what customers need to secure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong written and verbal communication, plus an organized approach to problem solving.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice to have: basic proficiency in a scripting language such as Python, JavaScript, or another modern language.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice to have: prior experience in a support, solutions engineering, or technical account role for AppSec, CI, or DevSecOps products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice to have: a security certification such as Security+, CSSLP, or CEH.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice to have: a Project Management Professional (PMP) or CAPM certification, or equivalent project management coursework.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice to have: a Computer Science degree or equivalent programming background, and exposure to enterprise-scale web technologies and micro