rements while challenging partner performance where shared interfaces create risk.<br /><br /><strong>Key responsibilities - safety management and compliance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the operational health and safety management framework for the data center portfolio: policy, critical-risk standards, annual objectives, assurance calendar, risk registers, incident classifications, documentation and management reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interpret applicable occupational health and safety requirements with local specialists; translate them into site-level expectations, control plans and auditable evidence across different countries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead regular risk assessments, inspections and assurance reviews; prioritize findings by severity and exposure, assign owners and verify corrective actions have actually reduced risk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create consistent arrangements for site access, inductions, competency checks, contractor onboarding, safety briefings and refresher training, including evidence of completion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop meaningful leading and lagging indicators, including high-potential near misses, overdue critical actions, training coverage, contractor observations and incident trends; present clear recommendations to leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support supplier selection and contract reviews by defining appropriate safety requirements, escalation expectations and minimum standards for colocation and technical service partners.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key responsibilities - operational and technical risk</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide safety oversight for electrical work interfaces, energized equipment, isolation and lockout/tagout, switching coordination, arc-flash exposure and simultaneous activities in live data halls.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assess safe systems of work for heavy rack deliveries, lifting and rigging, material handling, battery systems, working at height, temporary works, confined spaces where relevant and high-density IT installation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review method statements, risk assessments, permits to work and job safety analyses for high-risk activities, ensuring that scope, boundaries, competence, emergency arrangements and hold points are understood.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with engineering teams on the risks introduced by direct-to-chip liquid cooling, CDUs, coolant handling, pressurized circuits, leak detection, hot surfaces and changing rack densities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participate in readiness reviews before energization, commissioning, major deployments and changes in operating configuration; confirm critical safety issues are resolved or escalated before work proceeds.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate emergency planning and drills with colocation operators and emergency responders for fire, evacuation, electrical incidents, coolant leaks, medical emergencies and loss of critical infrastructure.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key responsibilities - investigations and culture</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead or coordinate investigations of incidents, unsafe conditions and high-potential near misses involving Mistral activities; use structured causal analysis and share actionable learning across the portfolio.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Challenge the completeness and quality of provider or contractor investigations when Mistral personnel or equipment may be exposed; track preventive measures through verification.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coach engineers, managers and vendors to identify hazards early, stop unsafe Mistral-controlled work and raise concerns without hesitation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build strong partnerships with operations, construction, logistics, physical security, compliance and HR; communicate safety expectations clearly in written guidance, training and site discussions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide practical support to other regions during major incidents, rapid expansion or unusual operational risk.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What success looks like</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Critical activities are governed by clear, adopted controls and a consistent standard across sites.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High-severity findings are visible, owned and resolved; incident learning results in verified preventive action.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Site and contractor training, emergency readiness and compliance evidence are maintained and readily accessible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The safety program scales with infrastructure growth without creating unnecessary bureaucracy.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Minimum qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least 5 years of practical health and safety experience in operational, industrial, construction or mission-critical environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience implementing safety programs, contractor controls, inspections, risk assessments, investigations and training.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of occupational safety regulations and high-risk work controls; ability to coordinate country-specific requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication and influencing skills across technical teams, suppliers and senior stakeholders; fluent professional English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work regularly on site and travel between data center locations; valid driving licence where required for site access.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preferred qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Data center, manufacturing, power infrastructure or complex construction experience involving employees and multiple contractors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with electrical safety, critical mechanical systems, commissioning and work in live operational facilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recognized HSE qualification and familiarity with ISO 45001-based management systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with international portfolios, colocation operators and high-density IT or liquid-cooled systems.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your well-being, growth, and work-life balance. Benefits vary by country and may include healthcare coverage, parental leave, retirement plans, relocation support, wellness programs, meal and transportation allowances, and other location-specific perks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For the most up-to-date details on benefits available in your location, please refer to our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://app.notion.com/p/mistralai/Benefits-at-Mistral-36e6ba59a7fe836b93dd01737fcc27ef?source=copy_link">Benefits page</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Privacy Policy</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your privacy matters to us. You can learn more about how we handle your personal data in our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://legal.mistral.ai/terms/applicant-privacy-policy"><u>Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/mistralai/data-centre-safety-manager-paris-490474","tags":["Engineering & Infra"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1792734017},{"slug":"design-reliability-engineering-manager-paris-244688","company_name":"Mistral.ai","title":"Design & Reliability Engineering Manager","description":"<h2><strong>About Mistral</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral provides full-stack AI solutions: from frontier models to developer tools, applications, and compute. We partner with enterprises tackling the hardest problems across high-stakes industries like finance, manufacturing, defense, healthcare, and the public sector, co-creating customized AI systems that they can run on their terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a dynamic, collaborative team passionate about AI and its potential to transform society. Our diverse workforce thrives in competitive environments and is committed to driving innovation. Our teams are distributed between Europe, North America, Asia and the Middle East. We are creative, low-ego and team-spirited.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our mission</strong><br /><br />Shape the engineering foundations of Mistral AI’s next generation of compute capacity while improving the resilience of the infrastructure already in service. This role combines technical design leadership with field reliability engineering: you will establish demanding, practical requirements for colocation power and cooling, scrutinize proposed solutions and turn operating experience into better designs, safer changes and more reliable AI capacity.<br /><br /><strong>Operating context &amp; accountability</strong><br /><br />Mistral deploys high-density AI infrastructure in colocation facilities, where partners operate the underlying critical plant. You will be Mistral’s technical counterpart to providers, designers, commissioning specialists and internal IT and capacity teams. The position combines forward-looking design authority with hands-on technical investigation and portfolio reliability improvement. It requires depth in one core engineering discipline and the judgment to lead multidisciplinary decisions with specialist support.<br /><br /><strong>Key responsibilities — design and technical standards</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and continuously improve Mistral’s technical design criteria and colocation requirements for new facilities, expansions and retrofits, including availability objectives, failure domains, maintainability and operational flexibility.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate GPU platform roadmaps into measurable facility envelopes: IT load and transients, rack density, electrical topology, redundancy, cooling capacity, supply/return temperatures, flow, pressure, water quality and monitoring.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review utility and MV/LV arrangements, transformers, generators, UPS, switchgear, busway, protection coordination, earthing, power quality and metering for suitability under demanding AI loads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review mechanical and controls architecture, including chilled-water and heat-rejection systems, pumps, control sequences, CDU integration, leak detection, filtration, water treatment and cooling recovery scenarios.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead multidisciplinary reviews of single-line diagrams, P&amp;IDs, sequences of operation, design calculations, capacity models, failure-mode studies and proposed deviations; document risks and decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participate in site selection, technical due diligence, provider RFPs, design milestones and commercial technical schedules, challenging assumptions before they become delivery constraints.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define design review and exception processes that balance performance, resilience, deployment speed, efficiency, capital cost and long-term operability.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key responsibilities — commissioning and delivery assurance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with delivery and commissioning teams to define functional and integrated testing requirements, acceptance criteria, evidence packages and outstanding-defect management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Validate that electrical and cooling infrastructure can support the contracted AI load envelope under normal, maintenance and credible fault conditions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review test scripts and results for loss of utility, UPS/generator transitions, cooling component failures, controls faults, CDU interface events and staged restoration where applicable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure operational handover includes accurate drawings, asset and interface registers, monitoring points, setpoints, maintenance constraints, emergency procedures and unresolved risk ownership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support live-site changes and capacity upgrades with a disciplined review of impact, sequencing, rollback plans and operational readiness.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key responsibilities — field reliability and root-cause analysis</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a technical escalation point for recurring or high-impact electrical, mechanical and controls incidents across operational colocation sites.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analyze alarms, BMS/EPMS trends, event sequences, power-quality records, cooling telemetry, commissioning findings and maintenance evidence to distinguish symptoms from systemic causes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead or challenge technical root-cause investigations with colocation partners, including common-mode failures, protection miscoordination, thermal instability, control logic, hydraulic performance and hidden capacity limitations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop risk-ranked corrective actions and reliability improvement programs; validate effectiveness through evidence and post-change monitoring.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify fleet-wide patterns and feed lessons learned into reference designs, acceptance tests, technical specifications and provider governance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review maintenance and change proposals that create material exposure to compute availability, providing clear technical recommendations and escalation where required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key responsibilities — collaboration and leadership</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with IT hardware, network and platform teams to understand the operational consequences of rack-level and cluster-level failure domains.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Influence colocation providers, consultants and OEM partners through technically rigorous, fact-based reviews without relying on direct operational authority.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Present design trade-offs, reliability risks and investment recommendations in language accessible to engineering leadership and business stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop reusable standards, technical playbooks and engineering knowledge sharing to support consistent decisions across a rapidly expanding portfolio.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What success looks like</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">New capacity is accepted against well-defined electrical, thermal and resilience criteria with transparent technical exceptions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design risks are identified early, reducing late changes, stranded capacity and avoidable operational constraints.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Repeat incidents and unresolved critical engineering defects decrease as corrective actions are verified.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Field experience produces measurable improvements to future designs and live-site operating resilience.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Minimum qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least 8 years in mission-critical data center design, engineering, commissioning or technical reliability, including responsibility for complex technical decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Degree in electrical or mechanical engineering, or equivalent professional experience, with deep knowledge in one discipline and strong working knowledge of the other.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated expertise in critical power and cooling architecture, redundancy, failure-mode analysis and operational risk management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience reviewing engineering drawings, calculations, commissioning evidence and root-cause analyses, and coordinating technical specialists.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to influence colocation providers and cross-functional stakeholders; excellent English communication and willingness to travel.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preferred qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with AI/HPC infrastructure, high-density accelerator platforms and direct-to-chip liquid cooling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of CDUs, facility-to-technology cooling interfaces, hydraulic performance, cooling-water quality and leak management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with electrical protection/selectivity, power quality, controls sequences, integrated systems testing and BMS/EPMS analytics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience creating technical standards across multiple sites or providers, including design deviations and fleet-wide reliability improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional engineering registration or equivalent technical credentials.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your well-being, growth, and work-life balance. Benefits vary by country and may include healthcare coverage, parental leave, retirement plans, relocation support, wellness programs, meal and transportation allowances, and other location-specific perks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For the most up-to-date details on benefits available in your location, please refer to our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://app.notion.com/p/mistralai/Benefits-at-Mistral-36e6ba59a7fe836b93dd01737fcc27ef?source=copy_link">Benefits page</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Privacy Policy</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your privacy matters to us. You can learn more about how we handle your personal data in our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://legal.mistral.ai/terms/applicant-privacy-policy"><u>Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/mistralai/design-reliability-engineering-manager-paris-244688","tags":["Engineering & Infra"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1792734017},{"slug":"critical-infrastructure-engineering-lead-paris-468025","company_name":"Mistral.ai","title":"Critical Infrastructure Engineering Lead","description":"<h2><strong>About Mistral</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral provides full-stack AI solutions: from frontier models to developer tools, applications, and compute. We partner with enterprises tackling the hardest problems across high-stakes industries like finance, manufacturing, defense, healthcare, and the public sector, co-creating customized AI systems that they can run on their terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a dynamic, collaborative team passionate about AI and its potential to transform society. Our diverse workforce thrives in competitive environments and is committed to driving innovation. Our teams are distributed between Europe, North America, Asia and the Middle East. We are creative, low-ego and team-spirited.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our mission</strong><br /><br />Serve as Mistral AI’s senior technical authority for critical electrical, mechanical and life-safety infrastructure across assigned colocation sites. Protect the availability of high-density AI compute by identifying technical risks before they become incidents, challenging infrastructure operating practices and verifying that power and cooling systems perform within agreed requirements.<br /><br /><strong>Operating context &amp; accountability</strong><br /><br />Working with Engineering Operations leadership, IT Operations, hardware partners and colocation providers, you will provide hands-on technical assurance across a site or cluster. You will assess provider performance, advise on critical decisions, support incident response and ensure operational learning drives durable improvements. The role focuses on technical oversight and influence rather than direct management of the colocation provider’s maintenance workforce.<br /><br /><strong>Technical assurance and operational risk</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and maintain the site technical risk register, including electrical and mechanical single points of failure, maintenance exposure, redundancy limitations, cooling capacity, liquid-cooling interfaces and common-mode failure scenarios.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assess the resilience of utility connections, MV/LV distribution, transformers, generators, UPS, switchgear, busways, protection systems, pumps, cooling plant, controls and monitoring against the contracted operating envelope.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review provider preventive maintenance strategies, schedules, critical asset condition and outstanding defects; identify maintenance deferrals and vulnerabilities that may affect AI compute availability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Critically review high-risk methods of procedure, electrical switching and isolation plans, planned impairments, work sequencing, contingency measures, rollback plans and restoration criteria.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Validate the completeness and quality of technical documentation, including single-line diagrams, P&amp;IDs, operating sequences, alarm matrices, capacity records, asset registers and operating procedures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use BMS/EPMS trends, alarms, power-quality records and cooling telemetry to identify abnormal operating conditions, capacity constraints and deteriorating resilience before service is affected.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Incident response, investigations and reliability</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a senior engineering escalation point during major infrastructure incidents; rapidly assess failure domain, remaining redundancy, safety implications, likely IT impact and viable restoration options.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate technical information across the colocation provider, Mistral IT Operations and OEM partners, ensuring accurate incident timelines, risk communication and controlled return to service.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review and challenge root-cause analyses, distinguishing immediate triggers from underlying design, maintenance, controls, process and organizational contributors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and follow up corrective and preventive actions, requesting evidence of implementation and verifying that recurring failure modes have been addressed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify systemic trends across sites and share lessons learned with engineering design, commissioning and regional operations teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support emergency response planning and tabletop exercises covering loss of utility, cooling failures, liquid leaks, fire/life-safety events and critical equipment failures.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Capacity delivery, commissioning and change control</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participate in design and constructability reviews for expansions, retrofits and new AI deployments; flag operational, maintainability and resilience concerns early.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review commissioning and integrated systems testing plans, including power transfers, redundancy scenarios, controls failure modes, cooling recovery and operational readiness criteria.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Challenge test results and acceptance evidence against defined electrical, thermal and operational requirements; track unresolved technical issues through handover.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with IT Operations on rack power and thermal limits, direct-to-chip liquid cooling, coolant distribution unit boundaries, leak response and load-restoration dependencies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assess proposed changes to critical infrastructure, including concurrent maintenance, controls updates and brownfield works; recommend safeguards and escalation where exposure is unacceptable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide technical coaching to internal stakeholders, contribute to engineering standards and support recruitment and knowledge sharing as the portfolio expands.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Success measures</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Critical technical risks are identified early, prioritized and reduced through verified mitigation actions, supporting Mistral’s availability objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High-risk maintenance and infrastructure changes receive timely, evidence-based technical review with clear mitigations and escalation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Major incidents are diagnosed accurately, communicated effectively and followed by robust root-cause analysis and verified corrective actions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">New and expanded capacity meets agreed redundancy, electrical, cooling and operational acceptance requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Repeat failures, unresolved high-severity defects and preventable technical deviations decrease over time.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Minimum qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5–7+ years in critical facilities engineering, commissioning, data center operations or technical assurance in high-availability environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong practical knowledge of critical electrical infrastructure (UPS, generators, MV/LV distribution, switchgear and protection) and mechanical systems (cooling plant, pumps, controls and heat rejection).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to review single-line diagrams, operating sequences, technical procedures, maintenance plans, commissioning evidence and root-cause analyses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated experience troubleshooting complex infrastructure incidents and influencing external technical teams without direct line authority.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear written and verbal English communication, sound judgment under pressure and willingness to travel and participate in incident escalation as needed.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preferred experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full technical governance, multi-site operations or mission-critical facilities serving high-density AI/HPC workloads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with direct-to-chip liquid cooling, CDUs, facility/technology cooling interfaces, water quality, leak detection and rack-level thermal management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integrated systems testing, EPMS/BMS trend analysis, protection coordination, failure-mode reviews and cross-site engineering standardization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience partnering with hardware OEMs, design engineers, commissioning teams and infrastructure providers during live-site expansion.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your well-being, growth, and work-life balance. Benefits vary by country and may include healthcare coverage, parental leave, retirement plans, relocation support, wellness programs, meal and transportation allowances, and other location-specific perks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For the most up-to-date details on benefits available in your location, please refer to our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://app.notion.com/p/mistralai/Benefits-at-Mistral-36e6ba59a7fe836b93dd01737fcc27ef?source=copy_link">Benefits page</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Privacy Policy</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your privacy matters to us. You can learn more about how we handle your personal data in our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://legal.mistral.ai/terms/applicant-privacy-policy"><u>Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a