, liquid-cooled systems — with new sites under development in France and beyond.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hardware here is not someone else's problem. As part of a small on-site team, you carry responsibility for it end to end.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> On-site at one of our data center in Bessé-sur-Braye, Pays de la Loire.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you'll do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Diagnose &amp; repair</strong> server and cluster hardware: CPUs, memory, drives, NICs, GPUs, PSUs, and interconnect problems (switches, cables, transceivers; Ethernet/InfiniBand).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Intervene safely</strong> — power-off/lockout, ESD discipline, pre/post-work checklists, tidy and safe work areas.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Capture everything</strong> — photos, serials, test results; open, update and close tickets with notes the next engineer can act on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manage parts</strong> — receive, label and track inventory; run RMAs and coordinate with vendors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Help us get better</strong> — feed recurring anomalies into monitoring, alerts and SOPs; contribute small scripts (Python/Bash) if you have those skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be a good teammate</strong> — clear status updates, honest handovers, and respect for the people depending on the cluster.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About you</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on comfort in data centers or server hardware — you can (or will quickly learn to) work cleanly in racks: rails, cabling, labeling, mounting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Disciplined and meticulous: checklists aren't bureaucracy to you, they're craftsmanship.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical electrical basics: power-off procedures, PPE, short-circuit risk awareness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Basic Linux (boot checks, logs) — scripting is a plus, not a requirement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Physically able to work in racks (lift, mount, maneuver) in a data center environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable in a 24/7 operation, including a rotating on-call with emergency response expectations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Driver's licence (B) for travel between our sites.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Even if you don't match every criterion</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Many of our best hardware engineers came from research labs, telecoms, IT services or the military. If you are rigorous, curious and genuinely motivated by hardware at scale, we would be glad to hear from you — we assess demonstrated scope rather than keyword matching.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Nice to have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">HPC/AI/cloud production experience at scale; large-fleet server install and maintenance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Networking fundamentals (Ethernet/InfiniBand) beyond basics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vendor/RMA tooling, ticketing (Jira/ServiceNow), inventory systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Python/Bash automation for checks, capture, inventory or reporting.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your well-being, growth, and work-life balance. Benefits vary by country and may include healthcare coverage, parental leave, retirement plans, relocation support, wellness programs, meal and transportation allowances, and other location-specific perks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For the most up-to-date details on benefits available in your location, please refer to our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://app.notion.com/p/mistralai/Benefits-at-Mistral-36e6ba59a7fe836b93dd01737fcc27ef?source=copy_link">Benefits page</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Privacy Policy</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your privacy matters to us. You can learn more about how we handle your personal data in our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://legal.mistral.ai/terms/applicant-privacy-policy"><u>Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/mistralai/data-center-hardware-engineer-besse-sur-braye-pays-de-la-loire-150383","tags":["Engineering & Infra"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Bessé-sur-Braye, Pays de la Loire","created_at":1792734016},{"slug":"bid-project-manager-eu-nato-h-f-paris-482228","company_name":"Alta Ares","title":"Bid & Project Manager – EU & NATO (H/F)","description":"<h3>About Alta Ares</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Alta Ares is an air defense Neoprime. We build AI-guided interceptors to counter drones and cruise missiles, along with the software platform that powers them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our customers are NATO-aligned militaries and defense institutions, and our systems are regularly deployed during live exercises and operational demonstrations across Europe, the Middle East, and Asia.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2024, we have grown to 90 people, raised over $60M, and increased revenue 40× this year. We are now entering a new phase of international expansion, industrial scaling, fundraising, and product development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role &amp; Mission</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">NATO agencies &amp; EU programs are investing in counter-drone capability now, and Alta Ares answers a fast-growing flow of their tenders and calls for proposals. As Bid &amp; Project Manager in our EU, NATO &amp; Eastern Flank team, you turn each opportunity into a compliant offer, then into a project delivered on time. Your sales director owns the customer relationship and the commercial strategy; you own the offer and its delivery.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a one-programme job. You will run several bids and projects at once: a NATO bid, an EU grant proposal, and an RFI can land in the same week, and none of them can slip.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a demanding, high-ownership role. Deadlines do not move, the stakes are real, and the team will rely on you to hold the line. We are looking for someone who wants that responsibility.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bid Management - from first read to submission</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Screen and qualify opportunities with your sales director; prepare bid/no-bid decisions with risks, resources, and price on the table</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Break each tender down (NATO IFB or RFQ, EU call, RFP for a Nation through EU-NATO platforms such as NSPA or SAFE joint procurement) into a compliance matrix, a bid plan and clear owners</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and assemble the management, technical and compliance volumes with Engineering, Product, Finance and Legal</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organise the review gates and prepare the final price review with Finance; submit complete, compliant and on time, every time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the clarification rounds and support your sales director in negotiations through to contract signature</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>NATO &amp; EU Procurement - the rules of the game</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Master NSPA and NCIA procedures: Source File registration, declarations of eligibility, notifications of intent, IFBs and RFQs, basic ordering agreements and framework contracts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run EU grant proposals (European Defence Fund, EDIP): Funding &amp; Tenders portal, consortium building, Part A and Part B, lump-sum budgets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track national procurement rules and partners on the Eastern Flank through EU-NATO (Poland, Romania, the Baltic States…), e.g. via NSPA or SAFE joint procurement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain the bid library: company documents, CVs, past performance, standard answers, templates</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Project Delivery - from award to acceptance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn each award into a project: kick-off, plan, milestones, risks, budget and change control</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate engineering, production, demo and logistics teams, and partners, to deliver what we promised when we promised it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own customer reporting, deliverables and acceptance (FAT/SAT), with the documentation trail for invoicing and audits</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run several projects in parallel, each at a different stage</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Process &amp; Reporting</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the bid and project rhythm for the team: calendar, gates, templates, dashboards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review the status of every live bid and project weekly with your sales director: deadlines, compliance, risks, resources needed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">