&lt;p&gt;Actual compensation packages are based on several factors that are unique to each candidate, including but not limited to skill set, depth of experience, certifications, and specific work location. This may be different in other locations due to differences in the cost of labor. The total compensation package for this position may also include bonus, stock, benefits and/or other applicable variable compensation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Summit does not accept referrals from employment businesses and/or employment agencies in respect of the vacancies posted on this site. All employment businesses/agencies are required to contact Summit’s Talent Acquisition team at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ----- ----- obtain prior written authorization before referring any candidates to Summit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Summit Therapeutics Inc.&amp;nbsp;is an Equal Opportunity Employer and takes pride in creating and maintaining diverse environment. We do not discriminate in recruitment, hiring, training or promotion or any other employment practices for reasons of race, color, religion, gender, national origin, age, sexual orientation, marital or veteran status, disability, or any other legally protected status.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/summittherapeutics/senior-specialist-qa-ireland-united-kingdom-409994","tags":["Quality & RA CMC"],"job_types":[],"location":"Ireland, United Kingdom","created_at":1792756513},{"slug":"remote-systems-engineer-zurich-94036","company_name":"Exeon Analytics","title":"Systems Engineer","description":"<h4 style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#C0504D">80-100% | as soon as possible | Germany or Switzerland</span><br></strong></h4><h4 style="text-align:start;"><strong><br>About Exeon</strong></h4><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;">Exeon is a Swiss cyber security company based in Zurich. Since 2016, we have been protecting critical infrastructures, financial institutions and enterprises whose operations fully rely on IT through AI-powered analysis of network communication. This makes the most sophisticated cyberattacks visible – attacks conventional tools fail to detect.&nbsp;We combine Swiss excellence with a flexible, remote-first, and collaborative culture, supporting passionate, ambitious professionals devoted to solving cybersecurity challenges and driving continuous innovation.<strong><br></strong></p><h4 style="text-align:start;"><strong>What your impact will be like:</strong></h4><p class="MsoNormal">As a Systems Engineer in our Solutions team, you will help design the components and data flow of our core products: how data gets in, how deployments are configured and operated, and how everything scales across very different customer environments, many of them on-prem and air-gapped.&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal">You’ll split your time between building (ingestion pipelines, automation, tooling) and deploying and operating (working with customers to get Exeon running reliably in their environments), so your work shapes both scalability and customer success.</p><p class="MsoNormal">In particular, you will:</p><ul><li><p>Build tooling and automation to simplify the deployment, configuration, and lifecycle management of Exeon.NDR, Exeon.UEBA, log collection and supporting components&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Design, build, and maintain scalable log ingestion pipelines for a wide range of network and application log sources and formats, including parsing, normalization, and validation&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Deploy and operate Exeon in customer environments (on-prem, private cloud, and hybrid), including sizing, performance tuning, and troubleshooting complex issues&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Work with customers to understand their data sources, infrastructure constraints, and security needs, and translate these into clear requirements for product and engineering teams&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Contribute to customer support, documentation, and runbooks alongside your Solutions colleagues</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>What you can expect from us:</strong></p><p>Exeon offers an open company culture that values and encourages diversity, teamwork and a growth mindset. Our goal is to provide our employees with an exciting, supportive and motivating environment for personal growth and career development while ensuring that our team maintains a healthy work-life balance. We strive to achieve this by offering:</p><ul><li><p>An exciting and impactful job in a fast-growing Swiss cyber tech company expanding across Europe with manifold opportunities to shape your professional profile.</p></li><li><p>Working in close collaboration with our interdisciplinary team and learning from our Security Experts, Data Scientists, and Business Professionals.</p></li><li><p>Taking over responsibilities quickly and help shape and promote a cutting-edge security software.</p></li><li><p>A high degree of trust, independence and flexibility, also in terms of working hours and place of work (remote or in the office).</p></li><li><p>A competitive salary and appealing benefits package.</p></li></ul> <br> <p><strong>What you bring along:</strong></p><p>We are looking for a proactive, self-motivated and enthusiastic cyber security professional who is comfortable in a high-paced start-up environment and who shares <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://exeon.recruitee.com/our-values">our values.</a> You should be confident with solving problems independently and communicating easily with both internal teams and directly with customers. You should also:</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">3-5 years of experience in systems engineering, data engineering, platform/infrastructure engineering, or a similar role&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Working knowledge of network and application security and the telemetry relevant to detection&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">UNIX/Linux experience, including networking, troubleshooting, and performance tuning in containerized deployments (Docker and/or Kubernetes)&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Strong programming skills in Python and Bash (or comparable languages), with a focus on automation and maintainable, production-quality code&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Hands-on experience designing and operating data ingestion pipelines (e.g. syslog, Logstash/Fluentd/Vector, Elastic stack, or similar), including handling heterogeneous formats and high volumes&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Comfortable with working in a largely remote team where clear communication is key to successful collaboration and impact. We are an English-speaking team but German fluency is appreciated when communicating to some customers&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">Degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or equivalent practical experience</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal"><br>Nice to have:</p><ul><li><p class="MsoNormal">Solid understanding of network and application security fundamentals, common attack patterns, and the log and telemetry sources that matter for detection&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Experience with SIEM, SOAR, or detection platforms (e.g. Splunk, Sentinel, Elastic Security), or as a detection engineer or security analyst&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Familiarity with network telemetry such as NetFlow/IPFIX, Zeek, or Suricata, and frameworks like MITRE ATT&amp;CK&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">Prior customer-facing or professional services experience.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/exeon-analytics/remote-systems-engineer-zurich-94036","tags":["Support & Engineering","Remote"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1792756292},{"slug":"ict-system-engineer-developer-80-100-zug-273029","company_name":"OBRO AG","title":"ICT System Engineer & Developer 80-100 %","description":"<p>Du liebst die Abwechslung und willst Dich nicht zwischen Systembetrieb und Softwareentwicklung entscheiden müssen? Bei uns kannst Du beides! Wir suchen eine strukturierte Persönlichkeit, die unsere IT-Infrastruktur im Griff hat und gleichzeitig neue Softwarelösungen mitgestaltet.</p>
<p>Wir wachsen und verstärken deshalb unser vierköpfiges ICT-Team per sofort oder nach Vereinbarung mit einem neuen Teammitglied im Pensum von 80 bis 100 %. Gemeinsam betreuen wir die IT unserer Firmengruppe mit mehreren Mandanten, mit über 100 Benutzerinnen und Benutzern an mehreren Standorten. Ob Dein Fundament in der Systemtechnik oder in der Applikationsentwicklung liegt: Wenn Du für moderne Technologien brennst, wollen wir Dich im Team haben.</p>
<h2>Aufgaben</h2>
<p><em>ICT Operation & Netzwerke</em></p>
<ul>
<li>Du stellst den stabilen Betrieb der IT-Umgebungen unserer gesamten Firmengruppe sicher, insbesondere Windows Server und Clients, Virtualisierung sowie Managed Security Services.</li>
