 and the business team. </p><p><strong>Lead what comes next</strong>: With the CEO and CTO, you set the software direction and lead development of future products. </p><p><strong>Our stack:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Backend:</strong> Python, FastAPI, PyTorch</p></li><li><p><strong>Frontend: </strong>React, TypeScript</p></li><li><p><strong>Hardware: </strong>C/C++, STM32 microcontrollers, Beckhoff PLCs</p></li><li><p><strong>Database: </strong>PostgreSQL (TimescaleDB)</p></li><li><p><strong>DevOps & Cloud: </strong>Linux, Docker, AWS, Grafana</p></li></ul><h2>What we are looking for</h2><p><strong>Required:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Education</strong>: MSc or PhD in Computer Science, Robotics, Electrical or Mechanical Engineering, or similar.</p></li><li><p><strong>Python</strong>: This is a must. You write clean Python that runs in production, on real systems.</p></li><li><p><strong>Embedded & Hardware: </strong>Shipped C/C++ on microcontrollers running on physical hardware; comfortable working with sensors, actuators, and basic electronics.  </p></li><li><p><strong>Applied AI & Control:</strong> Understanding of modern control and ML/RL methods, with hands-on PyTorch experience applied to physical or dynamic systems.</p></li><li><p><strong>Cloud & data</strong>: You are comfortable with PostgreSQL, Docker and AWS.</p></li><li><p><strong>Leadership attitude</strong>: You take ownership, make decisions, and want to grow as a leader.</p></li><li><p><strong>Languages</strong>: English. German is a big plus.</p></li><li><p><strong>Hybrid setting</strong>: You will be expected to be on-site at least three days per week, and sometimes at customers’ locations, to work on real products.</p></li><li><p><strong>Availability</strong>: 100%, as soon as possible.</p></li><li><p><strong>Work-permit: </strong>You need the right to work in Switzerland for this position.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Preferred:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Startup experience: </strong>You have worked in a startup before and know what that means.</p></li><li><p><strong>Building modeling and control: </strong>You have prior experience handling building data, modeling building dynamics, and developing building controllers; ideally with ML and RL tools. </p></li><li><p><strong>Frontend: </strong>React and TypeScript.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Mindset:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Hands-on:</strong> You lead, and you still do the hard work yourself.</p></li><li><p><strong>Fast:</strong> You are pragmatic and iterate quickly. Things break, and plans change, and that doesn't scare you.</p></li><li><p><strong>Purpose:</strong> You care about climate and want to make buildings smarter.</p></li></ul><h2>Benefits</h2><p><strong>Impact:</strong> Your code runs on real buildings. You see the result of your work.</p><p><strong>Ownership:</strong> A key role with a real say in our product and technology, and room to grow with the company.</p><p><strong>Flexibility:</strong> Hybrid work and flexible hours. We like being in the Zurich office together, so plan for regular office days.</p><p><strong>Team:</strong> A small, skilled, and down-to-earth team that helps each other out.</p><p><strong>The reality:</strong> We are a startup. It is often messy; things rarely work the first time, and the workload is real. In return, you get a lot of freedom and responsibility from day one.</p><h2>Sounds like you?</h2><p>Send us your CV and a short document instead of a classic cover letter. It doesn’t need to be long, just enough for us to understand who you are and where you stand. Please cover these points:</p><ul><li><p><strong>About you:</strong> A short description of yourself.</p></li><li><p><strong>Proud of:</strong> One thing you are really proud of, in a few sentences.</p></li><li><p><strong>Startup:</strong> Why do you fit a startup?</p></li><li><p><strong>Software meets hardware:</strong> Your experience where software and hardware come together.</p></li><li><p><strong>J