ment are key pillars of SkyCell.</p><p>🏆 Award-Winning Culture: Join a workplace recognized for its commitment to excellence with a ‘Great Place to work’ award, as well as a Platinum Ecovadis rating highlighting our sustainability and employee well-being.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>What You'll Do:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Design and implement embedded firmware for low-power IoT devices using C/C++ (RTOS or bare-metal)</p></li><li><p>Integrate wireless communication technologies such as BLE, LoRa or Cellular</p></li><li><p>Design, build and operate cloud-side ingestion pipelines and device fleet management systems for large-scale IoT deployments</p></li><li><p>Contribute to the design and deployment of cloud architectures for IoT integrations</p></li><li><p>Implement secure and reliable OTA update mechanisms for remote firmware management</p></li><li><p>Build and maintain CI/CD pipelines for firmware and cloud components (e.g. GitHub Actions)</p></li><li><p>Collaborate with colleagues across firmware, hardware and cloud teams</p></li><li><p>Troubleshoot complex system-level issues across device, connectivity and cloud layers</p></li><li><p>Contribute to architecture and process improvements based on emerging best practices</p></li></ul> <br> <p><strong>What You'll Bring:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science or a related field, or equivalent practical experience</p></li><li><p>Experience developing embedded firmware in C/C++ (RTOS or bare-metal), with a good understanding of common interfaces (I2C, SPI, UART)</p></li><li><p>Experience with wireless protocols (BLE, LoRa or Cellular) and IoT communication protocols and data formats (MQTT, HTTP/REST, CoAP, Protobuf, JSON)</p></li><li><p>Experience designing and operating cloud-based ingestion and device fleet management systems for connected IoT devices at scale</p></li><li><p>Experience implementing OTA updates in production systems</p></li><li><p>Proficiency in a 