or and control plasmas in real fusion devices, working side-by-side with leading plasma and control experts.</p></li><li><p>Great working conditions, located in Lausanne, Switzerland, a city and country known for its high quality of life.</p></li><li><p>Competitive salary and equity compensation, matched to level of seniority, and benefits including immigration assistance.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/fusionality/data-ml-engineer-fusion-data-lausanne-479954","tags":["Data Processing","Data Engineer"],"job_types":["Indefinite contract (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1792672271},{"slug":"technisch-support-engineer-the-hague-40820","company_name":"DeWarmte","title":"Technisch Support Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Bij DeWarmte maken we slimme en betaalbare warmtepompen waarmee we woningen van het gas af helpen. We ontwerpen onze producten zelf, assembleren ze in Utrecht en zorgen samen met onze installatiepartners dat ze bij steeds meer mensen thuis komen te staan.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Steeds meer woningen worden verwarmd met onze warmtepompen. En dat betekent dat we ook steeds meer installaties moeten monitoren, klanten ondersteunen en technische problemen oplossen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Daarom zoeken we een <strong>Technical Support Engineer</strong> die ons support team komt versterken.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je helpt klanten en monteurs bij technische vragen, onderzoekt storingen en zorgt dat onze warmtepompen optimaal blijven functioneren. Tegelijkertijd kijk je verder dan het probleem van vandaag. Waarom ontstaat een storing? Hoe kunnen we die in de toekomst voorkomen? En hoe kunnen we onze support slimmer organiseren?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Je lost dus niet alleen problemen op, maar helpt ons ook om onze producten en service steeds beter te maken.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Wat ga je doen?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Als Technical Support Engineer ben je een belangrijk aanspreekpunt voor technische vragen over onze warmtepompen. Je combineert technisch inzicht met klantcontact en werkt nauw samen met onze service-, product- en engineeringteams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Je helpt klanten en monteurs bij technische problemen</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je analyseert storingen en zoekt uit wat er aan de hand is, bijvoorbeeld door systeemdata en instellingen te onderzoeken.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je ondersteunt klanten telefonisch en per mail bij technische vragen en problemen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je helpt installateurs en servicemonteurs bij het oplossen van technische problemen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je past waar nodig instellingen van warmtepompen aan om hun prestaties te optimaliseren.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je schakelt servicemonteurs in wanneer een probleem niet op afstand kan worden opgelost en zorgt voor een goede overdracht.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Je helpt onze support steeds slimmer en beter te maken</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je herkent terugkerende problemen en denkt mee over structurele oplossingen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je maakt en verbetert technische documentatie, handleidingen en werkinstructies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je deelt inzichten uit de praktijk met onze product- en engineeringteams, zodat we onze warmtepompen verder kunnen verbeteren.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je denkt mee over hoe we onze processen en systemen kunnen verbeteren en automatiseren.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je komt terecht in een groeiend team waarin nog niet alles vastligt. Dat betekent dat je veel kunt leren, verantwoordelijkheid krijgt en zelf invloed hebt op hoe we werken.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Wat breng je mee?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We zoeken iemand die technisch nieuwsgierig is, graag problemen oplost en energie krijgt van het helpen van anderen. Je hoeft nog geen expert in warmtepompen te zijn. We leren je graag hoe onze systemen werken.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wat we belangrijk vinden:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je hebt een technische hbo-opleiding afgerond, bijvoorbeeld in werktuigbouwkunde, elektrotechniek of een vergelijkbare richting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je hebt technisch en analytisch inzicht en vindt het leuk om uit te zoeken hoe systemen werken.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je communiceert duidelijk en prettig, ook met mensen die minder technische kennis hebben.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je spreekt en schrijft goed Nederlands.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je bent zelfstandig, leergierig en neemt initiatief wanneer je ziet dat iets beter kan.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je vindt het leuk om zowel met techniek als met mensen bezig te zijn.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je bent minimaal 4 dagen per week beschikbaar.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mooi meegenomen, maar zeker geen vereiste:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ervaring met technische support, troubleshooting of klantcontact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kennis van warmtepompen, installatietechniek of andere technische systemen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ervaring met Python, data-analyse of het automatiseren van processen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Wat bieden wij jou?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een salaris van €3.000 tot €4.000 bruto per maand op basis van een fulltime dienstverband, afhankelijk van je ervaring.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">27 vakantiedagen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een pensioenregeling en reiskostenvergoeding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">De mogelijkheid om mee te delen in het succes van DeWarmte via onze Stock Appreciation Rights (SAR).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Veel ruimte om te leren, jezelf te ontwikkelen en verantwoordelijkheid te nemen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een informele werkomgeving met korte lijnen en collega's die graag samenwerken.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">De mogelijkheid om deels vanuit huis te werken, naast onze gezamenlijke kantoordagen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">En natuurlijk de kans om bij te dragen aan de energietransitie met producten die we zelf ontwikkelen en verbeteren.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Zin om mee te bouwen?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bij DeWarmte houden we van mensen die initiatief nemen, nieuwsgierig zijn en samen dingen beter willen maken. Je hoeft niet alles al te kunnen. Als je graag leert, verantwoordelijkheid neemt en energie krijgt van techniek en het helpen van mensen, maken we graag kennis met je.</p><hr><p>Compensation: €3K – €4K per month</p><ul><li> • €3K – €4K per month</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/dewarmte/technisch-support-engineer-the-hague-40820","tags":["Service"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"The Hague","created_at":1792777217},{"slug":"financial-director-the-hague-13916","company_name":"DeWarmte","title":"Financial Director","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Bij DeWarmte maken we slimme en betaalbare warmtepompen waarmee we woningen van het gas af helpen. We ontwerpen onze producten zelf, assembleren ze in Utrecht en zorgen samen met onze installatiepartners dat ze bij steeds meer mensen thuis komen te staan.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We groeien hard. Met een flinke groeispurt in het aantal aanvragen, een groeiende operatie in Nederland en onze eerste stappen in Duitsland breekt een nieuwe fase aan. Daarom zoeken we een Financial Director die onderdeel wordt van ons Management Team en de volledige verantwoordelijkheid neemt voor Finance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je wordt ons vierde MT-lid en werkt nauw samen met onze CEO, COO en People Director aan de verdere groei van DeWarmte.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je begint niet vanaf nul. Onze founders hebben een sterke financiële basis neergezet, met een geïntegreerd financieel model dat zich al tijdens meerdere financieringsrondes en due diligence-trajecten heeft bewezen. Nu zoeken we iemand die daarop voortbouwt en Finance naar een volgend niveau brengt.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>En daar krijg je alle ruimte voor.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je ontwikkelt je eigen visie op de financiële organisatie, stelt een financiële roadmap op en bouwt een schaalbaar team. Je vertaalt cijfers naar betere beslissingen, daagt bestaande aannames uit en helpt ons de juiste keuzes te maken terwijl we groeien.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We zoeken iemand die strategisch denkt, maar ook graag zelf de handen uit de mouwen steekt. Die het grotere plaatje ziet, maar net zo makkelijk de diepte ingaat om een financieel vraagstuk op te lossen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Wat ga je doen?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Als Financial Director ben je eindverantwoordelijk voor Finance én denk je als MT-lid mee over de koers van DeWarmte. Je bouwt voort op een sterke financiële basis en zorgt dat onze financiële organisatie klaar is voor de volgende groeifase.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Financiële strategie en business performance</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je ontwikkelt de financiële strategie en roadmap en vertaalt onze groeiambities naar concrete plannen en doelstellingen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je bent een strategische sparringpartner voor de founders en het MT. Je daagt aannames uit, beoordeelt kansen en helpt bij belangrijke investerings- en bedrijfsbeslissingen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je vertaalt financiële en operationele data naar inzichten die onze prestaties, winstgevendheid en besluitvorming verbeteren.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h3><strong>Financiële planning, control en financiering</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je neemt het eigenaarschap over ons geïntegreerde financiële model en bent verantwoordelijk voor budgettering, forecasting, scenarioanalyses en managementrapportages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je stuurt op cashflow, liquiditeit en werkkapitaal en zorgt dat we onze groei financieel kunnen blijven ondersteunen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je leidt de financiële voorbereiding van financieringsrondes en due diligence-trajecten en verzorgt de rapportages aan aandeelhouders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je waarborgt betrouwbare financiële administratie, rapportages en compliance, inclusief de verdere inrichting van onze Duitse activiteiten.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h3><strong>Bouwen aan een schaalbare finance-organisatie</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je ontwikkelt en leidt ons Finance-team, te beginnen met een Financial Controller, en stuurt onze externe financiële partners aan.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je verbetert processen en systemen en benut automatisering en AI om Finance slimmer en efficiënter te organiseren.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je zorgt voor heldere financiële verantwoordelijkheden en controles, zonder onnodige bureaucratie.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Je combineert dus strategie met uitvoering.</strong> De ene dag bespreek je met het MT de langetermijnstrategie, de andere dag duik je zelf in een forecast, werk je aan een financieringsvraagstuk of verbeter je een proces. Je voelt je comfortabel op beide niveaus.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Wie zoeken we?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We zoeken een Financial Director die financiële expertise combineert met ondernemerschap, leiderschap en een sterk gevoel voor de business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Wat je meebrengt:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ruime ervaring in senior financiële functies, bij voorkeur binnen een snelgroeiend bedrijf of een scale-up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een sterke achtergrond in zowel financial control als financial planning &amp; analysis (FP&amp;A).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ervaring met het vertalen van bedrijfsstrategie naar financiële plannen en concrete resultaten.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sterke financiële modelleervaardigheden en een goed begrip van P&amp;L, balans, cashflow en de operationele factoren die deze beïnvloeden.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ervaring in een hardware-, productie-, energie-, logistieke of andere werkkapitaalintensieve omgeving is een groot voordeel.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ervaring met financiering, fundraising, kredietfaciliteiten of due diligence is een plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Het vermogen om een financiële functie en team op te bouwen, zonder zelf de aansluiting met de dagelijkse praktijk te verliezen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Affiniteit met technologie, automatisering en AI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je beheerst zowel het Nederlands als het Engels op professioneel niveau.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Minstens zo belangrijk vinden we hoe je werkt:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Je denkt als ondernemer.</strong> Je kijkt verder dan de cijfers en begrijpt hoe Finance bijdraagt aan het succes van het hele bedrijf.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Je hebt een eigen visie.</strong> Je brengt ideeën mee, daagt de status quo uit en durft de founders en andere MT-leden kritisch tegen te spreken.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Je bouwt voort op wat goed werkt.</strong> Je neemt de tijd om de business en bestaande processen te begrijpen, voordat je bepaalt wat beter kan.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Je neemt eigenaarschap.</strong> Je wacht niet tot iemand je vertelt wat er moet gebeuren, maar ziet kansen, stelt prioriteiten en komt in actie.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Je combineert strategie met executie.</strong> Je krijgt energie van richting bepalen, maar net zo goed van zelf dingen voor elkaar krijgen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Je voelt je thuis in een scale-up.</strong> Je houdt van snelheid, kunt omgaan met verandering en onzekerheid en hebt geen volledig uitgewerkt plan nodig om vooruitgang te boeken.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Wat wij bieden</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een bruto maandsalaris tussen <strong>€7.500 en €9.000</strong> op basis van 40 uur, afhankelijk van je ervaring.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een sleutelrol binnen ons Management Team, met veel verantwoordelijkheid en directe invloed op de toekomst van DeWarmte.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">De ruimte om je eigen visie te realiseren en een financiële organisatie op te bouwen die met ons meegroeit.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deelname aan ons <strong>SAR-programma</strong>, waarmee je financieel meeprofiteert van de groei en het succes van DeWarmte.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een laptop en telefoon van de zaak.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Iedere dag een gezamenlijke lunch op kantoor.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regelmatige teamuitjes en borrels, waaronder onze jaarlijkse stranddag en wintersport.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een informele, ondernemende werkomgeving met korte lijnen, ambitieuze collega's en veel ruimte voor eigen initiatief.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Waarom DeWarmte?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Een echte plek aan tafel.</strong> Als vierde lid van ons Management Team heb je directe invloed op onze strategie, prioriteiten en toekomst.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>De kans om iets op te bouwen.</strong> Er ligt een sterke financiële basis, maar jij krijgt de ruimte en verantwoordelijkheid om de financiële organisatie, het team en de roadmap voor de komende jaren vorm te geven.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Een bedrijf midden in een belangrijke groeifase.</strong> In een fase van groeiende activiteiten en internationale ambities stap je in op een moment waarop sterk financieel leiderschap echt het verschil kan maken.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Een ondernemende, hands-on cultuur.</strong> We nemen snel beslissingen, geven mensen veel verantwoordelijkheid en zoeken continu naar manieren om beter te worden. We waarderen mensen die kritisch meedenken, elkaar helpen en plannen omzetten in actie.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Een missie die ertoe doet.</strong> We bouwen technologie die de energietransitie versnelt. Met jouw werk help je duurzame verwarming voor steeds meer huishoudens bereikbaar te maken.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Klaar om mee te bouwen?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We zoeken iemand die meer wil dan verantwoordelijk zijn voor de cijfers. Iemand die wil meebouwen aan een bedrijf, richting wil geven en blijvende impact wil maken.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Herken jij jezelf hierin? Dan maken we graag kennis met je.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><hr><p>Compensation: €7.5K – €9K per month</p><ul><li> • €7.5K – €9K per month</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/dewarmte/financial-director-the-hague-13916","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"The Hague","created_at":1792777217},{"slug":"senior-account-executive-benelux-netherlands-102698","company_name":"Theydo","title":"Senior Account Executive - Benelux","description":"<h1><strong>Help fix customer-centricity at scale</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Every company wants to become more customer-centric. At TheyDo, we make that ambition real. Our AI-powered journey management platform helps the world’s largest enterprises align around what matters most: their customers. By bringing scattered data and teams together, we empower smarter decisions and better experiences. Since 2019, global leaders across industries — including Ford, Cisco, Johnson &amp; Johnson, Siemens, Home Depot, and Lufthansa — have trusted us to scale journey management and deliver measurable impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by $50M from top-tier investors, including Blossom and 20VC, we are building a category-defining company. Our fully remote team of 100+ TheyDoers represents 30+ nationalities across 27 countries, united by a customer-led, people-first culture.<br /><br />Our mission is clear: Make journey management the most powerful business tool in the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re looking for a place where your work shapes the future of how companies operate, join us. Let’s build it together.<br /></p><h2><strong>The role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Journey management is becoming a must-have for the world's biggest companies, and TheyDo is the platform leading the category. Enterprises like Ford, Cisco, Vodafone and Pfizer already use TheyDo to understand their customers end to end and decide where to act.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Now we're going after the rest of Europes biggest brands, and we want you leading the charge. As a Senior Account Executive, you'll take a greenfield territory of enterprise accounts, open the doors, and land the new logos that define TheyDo's next chapter.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be based in the Benelux, working remotely and reporting to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/stephanariesen/">Stephan</a>. You'll join a team of 6 EU AEs, backed by SDR, Enablement and Customer Success colleagues across North America and Europe.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why this role, now</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The timing couldn't be better. Customer experience has moved into the boardroom, and enterprises want a way to turn it into decisions. TheyDo gives them that, and our customers are proving it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Europe is wide open. Your target list is full of companies that look just like the ones already buying from us, and most of them have never had a TheyDo conversation. We know what wins. Now we need someone to scale it and put their name on the logos that come next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is the moment to join: early enough to shape how we win, with the proof that we do.<br /></p><h2><strong>What you'll do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a role built around creating revenue that didn't exist before, not managing revenue that already does.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build your own pipeline. You'll start from a target list, not a book.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own a named list of Benelux enterprise accounts and decide where to focus, based on signal rather than hope</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Source most of your pipeline yourself through outbound, account-based plays with BDR and Marketing, events and executive networking</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Break into accounts with no existing relationship and find the senior person who owns the customer experience problem</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Win the first deal. You'll take a cold account all the way to signature.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run complex, multi-stakeholder cycles from first conversation through discovery, business case, procurement and close</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sell on value to C-level and VP buyers across CX, Product and Digital: a business case a CFO will sign, not a feature tour</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Land mid-to-high six-figure first deals, structured to expand, and hand them to Customer Success with the context to grow them</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape how we win. You'll help write the European playbook.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Refine our ICP, messaging and sales motion based on what you see in the field</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share buyer insight with Product so they can act on it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Forecast accurately and keep the team informed through clear async updates</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What this role isn't</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We'd rather be clear now than have the wrong person find out six months in.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">It isn't account management. You won't inherit renewals or an installed base to upsell. If most of your number has come from growing existing customers, this probably isn't your role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">It isn't inbound-led. Marketing and SDR will support you, but you'll be expected to create most of your own pipeline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">It isn't a finished machine. If you need fully built enablement, years of territory data and a playbook that tells you what to do next, you'll find this frustrating. If you want to help build those things, you'll find it energizing.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What we're looking for</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">4+ years closing B2B SaaS deals, with most of that in enterprise new-business roles selling into enterprise organizations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of exceeding annual quotas, where the majority of your closed revenue came from net-new logos you sourced yourself. Be ready to walk us through the numbers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven ability to land mid-to-high six-figure first deals with enterprises that weren't customers before.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling a platform or new-category product, where you had to create the need rather than respond to an RFP.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A value-selling methodology (MEDDPICC, Command of the Message or similar) you actually use, not just know.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence engaging C-level buyers, building consensus across stakeholders and navigating enterprise procurement, security and legal</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'd rather start with a blank target list than a handed-over book, and you're energized by a scale-up where the product and playbook move fast</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus points if you have experience selling to CX, Product, Digital or Design leaders</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>What we offer our permanent employees:<br /></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>💰 Competitive compensation and pre-IPO equity</strong> - we like to give our team members ownership with our stock package. When TheyDo succeeds, we all succeed!<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🌍 Fully remote working with flexible hours</strong> - we're staunch advocates for autonomy and flexibility.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🩺 Health Insurance benefit -</strong> at TheyDo our team’s health and wellbeing are a priority. We include tailored support for every employee, regardless of location.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🌴 Flexible holiday days</strong> – We love what we do and equally love taking a break. You'll have a minimum of 25 days of paid holiday per year (pro rata), in addition to public holidays and an extra three days during our annual company-wide winter shutdown in December.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🧠 Learning and Development budget</strong> we encourage everyone to take ownership and invest in their growth and development, providing financial support to benefit you in your role and career.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🧘‍♂️Wellbeing budget -</strong> nurture your mind and body. We’ll support you in looking after you, whether it's meditation, mindfulness, or a yoga/gym membership.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>👪 Paid parental leave</strong> - we'll ensure financial support and time off for you to bond with the newest little members of your family (6 months for the primary carer, and 6 weeks for the secondary carer - fully paid). We provide paid childcare leave when you need to take time out to help your little one recover.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>👨‍💻Home office or co-working support</strong> - choose your ideal workspace with our home office or co-working budget. Whether you prefer the comfort of your home office or the collaborative atmosphere of a co-working space, we've got you covered.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🗺️ Company events</strong> - we regularly connect in-person to strategise, reflect or simply have fun. Our most recent company retreats were held in Spain, Portugal and France.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>⚒️ Latest tech &amp; tools</strong> - MacBook Air or Pro, we want you to have the equipment that you’re most comfortable with. We use tools such as Gather, Slack, Notion, Loom, G:Suite and naturally TheyDo to work collaboratively and asynchronously.<br /><br />🚀 Continuous growth of our benefits package as we continue to grow in size</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>To any recruitment agencies, we appreciate you would like to support us but we do not accept any unsolicited CVs or introductions.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About TheyDo</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Our <strong>core values</strong> are the driving force behind every decision we make. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We <strong>‘Journey together’ </strong>along a path of collaboration and synchronization. In everything we do, we <strong>‘Own it’</strong>, never shying away from taking action or making decisions. Our <strong>‘Cloaks off’</strong> mentality ensures that transparency and integrity reign supreme. </em>We ‘<em><strong>Simply to accelerate</strong></em>', cutting through complexity to focus on what truly matters and moving forward with clarity and speed <em>Moreover, <strong>‘Customer Fueled’</strong> innovation is at the heart of our work, as we know that the success of our product is directly linked to how we involve our customers in the process.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">TheyDo is an equal opportunities employer. Our customers are diverse, and we believe our organisation should be, too. We nurture an inclusive culture where everyone feels equally important, no matter their background or status. We will never discriminate on the grounds of gender, civil status, family status, sexual orientation, religion, age, disability, education, or race.<br /><br />Our commitment to building a diverse and inclusive TheyDo includes making reasonable adjustments to the interview process. If you need any adjustments, please reach out to your Talent Partner. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you are a woman or part of an underrepresented group, we encourage you to apply. Even if you don’t check every box — your skills and perspective could be just what we need to succeed. We value diversity and know you bring something unique to the table!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-Remote</p><hr><p>Compensation: €130K – €170K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission</p><ul><li>Europe • OTE €130K – €170K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/theydo/senior-account-executive-benelux-netherlands-102698","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Netherlands","created_at":1792766421},{"slug":"senior-data-scientist-trust-safety-amsterdam-417890","company_name":"Vinteden","title":"Senior Data Scientist, Trust & Safety","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brief info about Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we&#39;re looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life – or even a third. &lt;br&gt;The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/marketplace&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Vinted Marketplace&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedgo&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Go&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedpay&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Pay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania&#39;s first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we&#39;ve grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Information about the position&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join Trust &amp;amp; Safety’s Actioning team, whose mission is to protect the Vinted community from harmful activities and content. The team owns critical mechanisms, including user reporting, moderation workflows, policy enforcement, and interventions against malicious users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will leverage your expertise in machine learning to research, design and implement new models for report and appeals prioritization, advanced sanctioning based on users&#39; suspicions, and automation of moderation decisions. This involves working closely with our engineering teams to develop robust pipelines for data handling, feature engineering, model training, deployment, and continuous improvement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Data Scientist, you will utilize advanced machine learning techniques to analyze text, images, and other data formats, tackling complex challenges to identify and address content that poses potential risks. You will champion best practices and methodologies, significantly enhancing the team&#39;s effectiveness and safeguarding Vinted. You will mentor others, influence the strategic direction for model development, and facilitate cross-functional collaborations to drive impactful results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this position, you’ll&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the research, development, and end-to-end lifecycle of production machine learning models that prioritize and automate actions on harmful marketplace entities at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play a crucial role in establishing and refining essential machine learning processes, such as data versioning, creating labeling pipelines, and ensuring high-quality data availability for effective model training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively collaborate across teams, particularly with Data Infrastructure and backend engineers, to develop and maintain scalable data pipelines and infrastructure, ensuring optimal performance and scalability of deployed models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence and contribute to the strategic roadmap for the Actioning team, collaborating with Decision Scientists to test, assess, and continuously improve new models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record in data science (4+ years of experience), with a strong foundation in machine learning, statistics, or computational mathematics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in both classical and deep learning techniques, and an adeptness in leveraging the latest tools and methodologies to solve complex problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building and deploying agentic AI applications or LLM-powered workflows that handle large traffic, balancing quality, latency, and cost efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the challenges involved in deploying, maintaining, and scaling real-time ML models in production, with a proven ability to address these challenges effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven capability to work with engineering teams, designing and implementing efficient data ingestion, feature engineering, and model training pipelines that support robust and reliable model deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving abilities, with a commitment to staying at the forefront of developments in machine learning and data science, driving innovation and thought leadership within the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to clearly communicate complex ideas and technical concepts to both technical and non-technical stakeholders, ensuring that technical elements are properly understood and integrated to deliver business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Past experience with fraud detection, harmful content detection or any other adversarial domain would be considered an advantage.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work perks&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to benefit from our share options programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days of paid annual leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Newest MacBook models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for you and your family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frequent team-building events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home office support: we provide IT workstation equipment and a personal budget of up to €540 for home workplace furniture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lunch benefit per working day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A personal monthly budget for shopping on Vinted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collective Defined Contribution Pension plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NS Business Card for your commute to the office by public transport&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company bike leasing scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly budget for a flexible benefits platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work from Home allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dog-friendly office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workation policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Better balance holidays with workdays by working remotely! Up to 90 days per year in the EU, of these, 21 days can be spent globally. For non-EU citizens, it&#39;s 21 days worldwide. This can be combined with time off for vacation or personal time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Individual learning budget&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each year, you’ll be given a learning budget (starting at €3,000), and a total of up to 10 working days over a 2-year period to support your personal and professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our hybrid model, with 2 recommended office days a week, gives you and your team the flexibility to decide if and when you want to work from home, and when to catch up in person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome applications from everybody, regardless of your background, identity, or life experiences. Job openings come with guides, not checklists. If you’re excited about a role, but don’t identify with every point in the ‘About you’ section, apply anyway – you might still be the perfect match!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual gross salary range for this position excluding 8% holiday pay is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€67.700&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€91.500 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/vinteden/senior-data-scientist-trust-safety-amsterdam-417890","tags":["Data Science & Analytics"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792756513},{"slug":"engineering-manager-amsterdam-260715","company_name":"GreenFlux","title":"Engineering Manager","description":"<p class="Paragraph SCXW160586995 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">The company</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW160586995 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">Smart Electric Vehicle Charging Solutions. That’s the business we are in!</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW160586995 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">GreenFlux offers a cloud-based charge point management SaaS (Software as a Service) solution. This software platform enables Charge Point Operators (CPOs) and e-Mobility Service Providers (eMSPs) to successfully launch their respective businesses. With its offering, GreenFlux plays a pivotal role in facilitating the uptake of electric vehicles and the renewable energy revolution.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW160586995 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">Our Development department is responsible for the technical design of new features, owns the architecture, and does technical operation. We are organised in agile end-to-end teams, working with well-defined and transparent processes. Our tech stack is centred around Microsoft .NET on Azure.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW160586995 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">To keep up with the rapid market and business expansion and to support the company’s dynamic growth, we are looking to bring an Engineering Manager to the team.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW160586995 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">The job</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW160586995 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">The Engineering Managers (internally referred to as Heads of Engineering) are responsible for the performance of our development teams and the quality of our platform. You will be responsible for line managing the engineers of up to three development teams, ensuring they have the right direction, skills, and support to deliver high-quality results. Besides this, you will contribute to improving our agile way of working and strengthening engineering practices throughout the Development department.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW115915184 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Key result areas include:</span></strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW115915184 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW115915184 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Leadership and accountability:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You are the hierarchical manager of the engineers in your teams and are accountable for growing those teams to become autonomous and highly performing. You set clear expectations, provide regular feedback, and are accountable for individual and team performance. You actively identify and address performance issues and skill gaps, coaching and developing engineers to become more self-sufficient and effective.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW115915184 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW115915184 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Delivery and execution:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You take responsibility for ensuring your teams deliver high-quality software in a predictable and efficient manner. You proactively manage risks, dependencies, and impediments, taking action when delivery or quality is at risk and driving improvements where needed.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW115915184 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW115915184 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Technical quality:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You use your technical background to assess and challenge engineering decisions, ensuring that software solutions meet the required standards for quality, reliability, scalability, and maintainability. You work closely with engineers and technical leads to promote sound technical decisions and address technical debt</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW115915184 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW115915184 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Continuous improvement:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You drive improvements in engineering processes, ways of working, and the adoption of modern technologies, practices, and tools. You identify opportunities to increase efficiency, improve delivery performance, and strengthen engineering quality across teams.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW115915184 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW115915184 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Team development:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You build and maintain high-performing teams by ensuring the right balance of skills, experience, and perspectives. You proactively identify development needs, support professional growth, and foster a culture of ownership, collaboration, and continuous learning.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW115915184 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW115915184 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Quality and documentation:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You promote strong engineering standards, effective quality control, and clear technical documentation to support the long-term stability and maintainability of our platform.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW115915184 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW115915184 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Strategic contribution:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You contribute to setting the strategic direction of the Development department, translating broader objectives into concrete improvements and actions within your teams.</span></p></li></ul> <br> <p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Requirements</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">We are looking for a strong and accountable engineering leader who combines a people-oriented approach with a clear focus on delivery, technical quality, and results. You empower your teams and create an environment where people take ownership of their work. You have a strong agile mindset without being dogmatic about tools and frameworks, and you know when to coach, challenge, or take decisive action to improve performance.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">You have</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">3+ years of experience as an Engineering Manager, preferably in a tech scale-up or SaaS environment.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">A solid background in software engineering, with the technical expertise to evaluate engineering decisions and assess software quality, reliability, scalability, and maintainability.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">Proven experience in leading engineering teams, setting clear expectations, managing performance, and addressing skill gaps through coaching, feedback, and development.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">A strong focus on delivery and execution, with the ability to take ownership of results, proactively manage risks, and drive improvements.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">Extensive knowledge of software development processes, modern engineering practices, and agile ways of working.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the confidence to challenge decisions, provide constructive feedback, and collaborate with different stakeholder groups.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">The ability t